{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ukka8W39bHJHaqCgP2JHQ2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '跨架构证据被质疑为不充分或 trivial。Reviewer 论证 R² exit collapse 是 decoder-only\n2\t  架构的通用表征压缩 而非 VLA-specific effect（\"any supervised fine-tuning on decoder-only LLM\n3\t  would produce similar exit-layer information loss\"）。OpenVLA Spatial 无明显 exit collapse（RUNNING\n4\t  实验结果弱），矩阵空洞（NORA Object/Long 缺失）使 \"architecture-independent\" claim 站不住。D090 的 base-model-dependent\n5\t  发现被解读为 \"contribution 只剩 exit collapse 一个 training-induced effect，太薄\"。三层级梯度仅 1 个\n6\t  Tier-2 数据点（OpenVLA OXE）， 被驳为 post-hoc narrative。Behavioral validation 完全缺失在 CoRL（robotics\n7\t  venue）被视为 near-fatal。 Reframe 方向：从 \"architecture-independent routing signature\"\n8\t  转为 \"systematic diagnostic framework for VLA internal representations\"。C1 (framework)\n9\t  升为主要贡献，R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity 降为 \"findings the framework reveals\"。增加 per-layer\n10\t  information flow entropy、cross-task transfer analysis 等 framework demonstration\n11\t  analyses 增强贡献厚度。\n12\t\n13\t  '\n14\timagined_experiments:\n15\t- name: SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\n16\t  plan_id: plan_001\n17\t  description: SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen\n18\t    vision encoder\n19\t  expected_results:\n20\t    siglip_projector_rsa: 0.615\n21\t    trained_with_inst_rsa: 0.488\n22\t    untrained_with_inst_rsa: 0.485\n23\t    dino_rsa: 0.388\n24\t    llm_degradation_delta: 0.127\n25\t  result_rationale: '数据已完成不变。但在 worst D095 下，此实验仅覆盖 OpenVLA 一种架构。Reviewer 攻击： \"SigLIP+DinoSigLIP\n26\t    projector 的 RSA=0.615 是 OpenVLA-specific 的 frozen encoder 观察。 TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision\n27\t    的不同 encoder，NORA 用 InternViT——你们没测这些 encoder 的 RSA。 单架构 encoder analysis 不能 claim\n28\t    architecture-independent。\" 在 framework reframe 下， 此实验降为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上的\n29\t    case study\"，不再是 core contribution。 LLM degradation（0.615→0.488）本身仍有价值但被限定为 \"observed\n30\t    in Llama-2-7B backbone\"。\n31\t\n32\t    '\n33\t  tables:\n34\t  - title: SigLIP RSA Scope Limitation (Worst-Tier)\n35\t    columns:\n36\t    - Source\n37\t    - RSA\n38\t    - Architecture Coverage\n39\t    - Worst Interpretation\n40\t    rows:\n41\t    - - SigLIP+Proj\n42\t      - '0.615'\n43\t      - OpenVLA only\n44\t      - Cannot generalize to other VLA encoders\n45\t    - - VLA trained\n46\t      - '0.488'\n47\t      - OpenVLA only\n48\t      - Llama-2 specific LLM degradation\n49\t    - - VLA untrained\n50\t      - '0.485'\n51\t      - OpenVLA only\n52\t      - Random-init Llama-2 specific\n53\t    - - DINO\n54\t      - '0.388'\n55\t      - Standalone\n56\t      - Reference baseline, unaffected\n57\t  figures_description:\n58\t  - Bar chart 标注 'OpenVLA only' 在每个 bar 上方，突显 single-arch limitation\n59\t  analysis: 'Framework reframe 下此实验从 C1 core evidence 降为 Section 4.1 case study。 价值在于\n60\t    demonstrate framework 的 encoder-LLM decomposition 能力，而非 claim 本身。 Reviewer 不会因此给分但也不会因此扣分——neutral\n61\t    contribution in worst tier。\n62\t\n63\t    '\n64\t- name: DINO baseline RSA\n65\t  plan_id: plan_002\n66\t  description: Standalone vision model 参照基线\n67\t  expected_results:\n68\t    dino_rsa: 0.388\n69\t    dino_action_R2: 0.687\n70\t    dino_subtask_auc: 0.972\n71\t  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst 档下 DINO 的角色不变——纯视觉 baseline。但 reviewer 可能用 DINO 的高\n72\t    action R²=0.687 攻击论文：\"DINO（self-supervised, 无 language, 无 action training） 的 action\n73\t    probe R² 已 0.687，你们声称的 VLA training-induced R² exit collapse 只是从 0.68 掉到 0.60——这可能只是\n74\t    fine-tuning 过程中正常的 representation compression， 任何 supervised fine-tuning 都会导致\n75\t    exit layer 表征质量下降。\"\n76\t\n77\t    '\n78\t  tables: []\n79\t  figures_description:\n80\t  - DINO 作为 'no-training baseline' 的 R²=0.687 标注在所有 cross-arch R² exit collapse 图上，质疑\n81\t    collapse 的意义\n82\t  analysis: 'DINO baseline 在 worst tier 被 reviewer 用来论证 exit collapse 的 trivial nature：\n83\t    如果未训练模型 R²=0.687 而训练后 exit R² 下降到 0.55-0.60，这可能只是 supervised learning 的通用 representation\n84\t    bottleneck 而非 VLA-specific routing。\n85\t\n86\t    '\n87\t- name: Per-layer RSA degradation curve\n88\t  plan_id: plan_003\n89\t  description: 追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\n90\t  expected_results:\n91\t    proj_rsa: 0.615\n92\t    trained_peak_rsa: 0.488\n93\t    trained_peak_layer: 9\n94\t    untrained_peak_rsa: 0.485\n95\t    untrained_peak_layer: 12\n96\t    proj_to_l1_drop: 0.13\n97\t    inverted_u_pattern: true\n98\t  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下，inverted-U pattern 只在 OpenVLA (Llama-2) 上验证。\n99\t    TracVLA 和 NORA 的 RSA per-layer curve 未做（只做了 R² probe），所以 \"inverted-U is architecture-independent\"\n100\t    无法 claim。Reviewer：\"RSA inverted-U 可能是 Llama-2 的 32 层架构特有的——Phi-3-mini 同为 32 层但\n101\t    tokenization 不同，Qwen2.5-VL 是 36 层 且 GQA 架构，per-layer dynamics 可能完全不同。\" 此外 CKA\n102\t    反转（plan_009）使 RSA 本身作为 metric 的 authority 被削弱。\n103\t\n104\t    '\n105\t  tables:\n106\t  - title: RSA Inverted-U Architecture Coverage\n107\t    columns:\n108\t    - Architecture\n109\t    - RSA Per-Layer Done?\n110\t    - Pattern\n111\t    - Worst Interpretation\n112\t    rows:\n113\t    - - OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\n114\t      - 'Yes'\n115\t      - Inverted-U\n116\t      - Only confirmed case\n117\t    - - TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\n118\t      - 'No'\n119\t      - Unknown\n120\t      - Cannot claim generalization\n121\t    - - NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\n122\t      - 'No'\n123\t      - Unknown\n124\t      - Cannot claim generalization\n125\t  figures_description:\n126\t  - Per-layer RSA curve 只有 OpenVLA 一条线，旁边标 '?' 表示其他架构未验证\n127\t  analysis: 'Framework reframe 下，inverted-U 成为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上发现的 pattern\"\n128\t    而非 \"architecture-independent finding\"。可以保留为 case study 但不能 claim generality。 补救路径：增加\n129\t    TracVLA/NORA 的 per-layer RSA 分析作为 framework demonstration。\n130\t\n131\t    '\n132\t- name: Output head analysis\n133\t  plan_id: plan_004\n134\t  description: SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\n135\t  expected_results:\n136\t    vision_projector_cos_sim: 1.0\n137\t    llm_rel_change_range:\n138\t    - 1.22\n139\t    - 1.37\n140\t    head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n141\t    shallow_adaptation_gate: FAIL\n142\t  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下，此实验对 framework 贡献有价值——它证明 framework 能 区分 frozen\n143\t    和 trainable 组件。但 reviewer 可能指出：\"这是 trivial verification—— OpenVLA 的训练代码明确 freeze\n144\t    了 vision encoder，你们只是验证了代码做了它说的事。 这不是 experimental finding，是 implementation confirmation。\"\n145\t    在 framework paper 中， 这降为 Section 3 的 methodology validation paragraph，不占独立篇幅。\n146\t\n147\t    '\n148\t  tables: []\n149\t  figures_description: []\n150\t  analysis: 'Worst tier 下此实验贡献接近零——reviewer 视为 trivial。但在 framework reframe 下 可以包装为\n151\t    \"framework 的 component attribution 能力 demonstration\"：展示 framework 如何分离 encoder/projector/LLM\n152\t    各组件的贡献。贡献在方法论而非 finding。\n153\t\n154\t    '\n155\t- name: 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证\n156\t  plan_id: plan_005\n157\t  description: 系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained 表征结构\n158\t  expected_results:\n159\t    trained_vs_untrained_delta: 0.003\n160\t    all_methods_consistent: true\n161\t    cross_benchmark_replicated: true\n162\t  result_rationale: 'Orphaned 但子实验完成。Worst D095 下，trained ≈ untrained 的 RSA 结论仍成立\n163\t    但意义被 D090 reinterpret：Reviewer 说 \"trained ≈ untrained 在 distributed representation\n164\t    (RSA/R²) 上不奇怪——frozen encoder 输出相同 L0 features，LLM 的 fine-tuning 主要影响 exit layer\n165\t    action head，中间层表征 naturally preserved。 这是 transfer learning 的常识，不需要 6 种方法来验证。\"\n166\t    在 framework paper 中， 6 methods consistency 仍是 methodology 亮点——展示 framework 的 multi-method\n167\t    triangulation 能力。但 finding 本身被视为 expected。\n168\t\n169\t    '\n170\t  tables:\n171\t  - title: 6 Methods Consistency (Worst-Tier Reinterpretation)\n172\t    columns:\n173\t    - Method\n174\t    - Trained-Untrained Delta\n175\t    - Reviewer Interpretation\n176\t    rows:\n177\t    - - RSA\n178\t      - '0.003'\n179\t      - 'Expected: frozen encoder dominates'\n180\t    - - R² probe\n181\t      - '0.015'\n182\t      - 'Expected: similar L0 inputs'\n183\t    - - CKA\n184\t      - '-0.006'\n185\t      - 'Reversal: undermines RSA conclusion'\n186\t    - - Action probe\n187\t      - '0.045'\n188\t      - 'Marginal: routing exists but small'\n189\t    - - Delta probe\n190\t      - '0.011'\n191\t      - 'Expected: similar input structure'\n192\t    - - Classification\n193\t      - '0.001'\n194\t      - Trivially easy for both\n195\t  figures_description:\n196\t  - 6-method radar chart 显示 consistency，但加标注 'Expected under frozen encoder'\n197\t  analysis: 'Worst tier 下 6 methods consistency 从 \"strong evidence for Claim 3\" 降为\n198\t    \"thorough but unsurprising verification\"。Framework reframe 下，价值在于 demonstrate\n199\t    framework 的 multi-method coverage 而非 finding novelty。\n200\t\n201\t    '\n202\t- name: Instruction ablation\n203\t  plan_id: plan_006\n204\t  description: 去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\n205\t  expected_results:\n206\t    delta_with_vs_no_inst: 0.004\n207\t    gate_judgment: FAIL — instruction 无影响 on RSA\n208\t  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下，instruction 对 RSA 无影响是 OpenVLA-specific 观察。\n209\t    Reviewer：\"RSA 测量 image token 的几何结构，当然不受 instruction 影响——image tokens 在 causal\n210\t    mask 下看不到 instruction tokens，这在你们 C1 里已经承认是 structural guarantee。所以 Δ=0.004 不是\n211\t    finding，是 sanity check。\" 更严重的是，TracVLA 和 NORA 上未做此 ablation，所以即使从 framework demonstration\n212\t    角度也只是单架构。\n213\t\n214\t    '\n215\t  tables: []\n216\t  figures_description: []\n217\t  analysis: 'Worst tier 下从 \"Claim 3 evidence\" 降为 \"expected sanity check\"。 但在 framework\n218\t    paper 中，instruction ablation 仍可作为 framework 的 \"controlled manipulation\" capability\n219\t    demonstration，只是不能 claim novelty。\n220\t\n221\t    '\n222\t- name: 2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\n223\t  plan_id: plan_007\n224\t  description: 四条件全收敛验证\n225\t  expected_results:\n226\t    four_cell_range:\n227\t    - 0.48\n228\t    - 0.49\n229\t    bootstrap_ci_includes_0: true\n230\t    training_effect: 0.003\n231\t    instruction_effect: 0.004\n232\t  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下 2×2 矩阵仍是 clean experimental design 但 被视为 \"confirms\n233\t    the obvious\"。Reviewer：\"frozen encoder + causal mask 已经预测了这个 null result。你的 2×2\n234\t    design 很好但发现的是 expected outcome—— 这不是 contribution，是 verification。\" 在 framework\n235\t    paper 中，2×2 factorial design 可以作为 framework reusability 的 exemplar（\"researchers\n236\t    can apply this factorial approach to any VLA\"），但 the finding itself 不计分。\n237\t\n238\t    '\n239\t  tables:\n240\t  - title: '2×2 Matrix (Worst-Tier: Expected Null)'\n241\t    columns:\n242\t    - Condition\n243\t    - RSA\n244\t    - Reviewer Verdict\n245\t    rows:\n246\t    - - Trained + Inst\n247\t      - '0.488'\n248\t      - 'Expected: frozen encoder dominates'\n249\t    - - Trained - Inst\n250\t      - '0.489'\n251\t      - 'Expected: image RSA independent of text'\n252\t    - - Untrained + Inst\n253\t      - '0.485'\n254\t      - 'Expected: same encoder, same RSA'\n255\t    - - Untrained - Inst\n256\t      - '0.480'\n257\t      - 'Expected: null result confirmed'\n258\t  figures_description:\n259\t  - 2×2 heatmap 标注 'Expected null result under frozen encoder hypothesis'\n260\t  analysis: 'Framework paper reframe 下，2×2 matrix 的价值从 \"empirical finding\" 转为 \"exemplar\n261\t    of framework''s factorial design capability\"。论文可以说 \"our framework enables systematic\n262\t    2×2 factorial decomposition of training and instruction effects\"——贡献在方法论可复用性而非结果。\n263\t\n264\t    '\n265\t- name: Random instruction control\n266\t  plan_id: plan_008\n267\t  description: 随机/无意义 instruction 替代验证 RSA 不受 instruction content 影响\n268\t  expected_results:\n269\t    normal_rsa: 0.489\n270\t    random_rsa: 0.484\n271\t    shuffled_rsa: 0.483\n272\t    empty_rsa: 0.472\n273\t    max_absolute_delta: 0.017\n274\t    instruction_invariant: true\n275\t  result_rationale: '数据不变。与 plan_006/007 相同逻辑——causal mask 使 image token RSA 对 instruction\n276\t    天然不变。四种 instruction 条件下 Δ<0.02 是 expected 而非 surprising。 Worst D095 的关键攻击面不在此实验本身，而在于论文用了三个\n277\t    plan（006/007/008） 来验证一个 structurally guaranteed result，reviewer 会认为 \"过度验证 trivial\n278\t    prediction，浪费篇幅\"。在 8 页限制下这 3 个实验应压缩为 1 段。\n279\t\n280\t    '\n281\t  tables: []\n282\t  figures_description: []\n283\t  analysis: 'Framework reframe 下，random instruction control 与 006/007 合并为 \"three-way\n284\t    invariance verification\" 单段，作为 framework sanity check 的示范。占 0.5 段而非独立 subsection。\n285\t\n286\t    '\n287\t- name: CKA verification\n288\t  plan_id: plan_009\n289\t  description: CKA 指标验证 RSA 发现的 metric robustness\n290\t  expected_results:\n291\t    cka_ordering: untrained > trained > projector > DINO (反转 RSA)\n292\t    rsa_cka_dissociation: true\n293\t    linear_cka_last_preaction: 0.127\n294\t  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下 CKA-RSA dissociation 变得更致命。Reviewer： \"你们声称\n295\t    R² exit collapse 是 architecture-independent training effect， 但 CKA（另一种 representational\n296\t    similarity metric）显示 untrained > trained—— 即训练反而增强了 global structure。如果换个 metric\n297\t    就得到相反结论， 那 R² exit collapse 可能只是 metric artifact 而非 genuine information loss。\n298\t    你们怎么证明 R² 比 CKA 更能捕捉 ''action-relevant information''？\" 在 framework paper 中，metric\n299\t    dissociation 可以包装为 \"framework reveals metric-dependent conclusions\"——但这削弱了所有 quantitative\n300\t    findings 的 authority，因为 reviewer 会质疑每个 metric 的选择。\n301\t\n302\t    '\n303\t  tables:\n304\t  - title: 'Metric Ordering Reversal (Worst: Authority Crisis)'\n305\t    columns:\n306\t    - Metric\n307\t    - Ordering\n308\t    - Implication\n309\t    rows:\n310\t    - - RSA (geometric)\n311\t      - SigLIP > T > U > DINO\n312\t      - Training degrades geometry\n313\t    - - CKA (global)\n314\t      - U > T > SigLIP > DINO\n315\t      - Training preserves/improves structure\n316\t    - - R² (functional)\n317\t      - T_readout > DINO ≈ Proj > T_img\n318\t      - Training enables routing\n319\t    - - Reviewer question\n320\t      - —\n321\t      - Which metric is 'correct' for VLA evaluation?\n322\t  figures_description:\n323\t  - Triple ordering diagram 标注 '?' 在每条 ordering line 上——哪个 metric 才对？\n324\t  analysis: 'Worst tier 下 CKA dissociation 是双刃剑。Framework reframe 可以用它 作为 \"why we\n325\t    need multi-metric frameworks\"（方法论贡献），但这同时 undermine 了 R² exit collapse 作为 \"the\n326\t    architecture-independent signature\" 的 clean narrative。如果 exit collapse 只在 R² 下明显而\n327\t    CKA 下不成立， reviewer 会要求 \"architecture-independent claim 必须 metric-independent\"。\n328\t\n329\t    '\n330\t- name: LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展\n331\t  plan_id: plan_010\n332\t  description: 第三个 benchmark（LIBERO-Spatial）交叉验证\n333\t  expected_results:\n334\t    trained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.696\n335\t    trained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.675\n336\t    untrained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.673\n337\t    untrained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.635\n338\t    trained_exit_R2_delta: 0.04\n339\t    bootstrap_significance_p: 0.001\n340\t    cross_benchmark_consistency: partial\n341\t  result_rationale: 'LIBERO-Spatial 数据已部分完成（plan_010 status=preparing 但 registry 有结果）。\n342\t    Worst D095 下，此实验是 OpenVLA 的 within-architecture cross-benchmark， 不是 cross-architecture\n343\t    validation。Reviewer：\"你从 LIBERO-Goal 换到 LIBERO-Spatial 只是换了 task suite 而非换了 VLA\n344\t    架构——这不解决 RC4 的核心问题。\" 更关键的是，Spatial 的 exit R² delta 只有 0.04（vs Goal 的 0.069）， 说明\n345\t    exit collapse strength 是 task-dependent 的。Worst 解读： exit collapse 不是 fundamental\n346\t    property 而是 task difficulty proxy—— harder tasks (Spatial) 产生较弱 collapse 因为模型需要保留更多\n347\t    exit-layer information 来处理复杂空间推理。\n348\t\n349\t    '\n350\t  tables:\n351\t  - title: Cross-Benchmark Exit Collapse Comparison\n352\t    columns:\n353\t    - Benchmark\n354\t    - Trained Exit Delta\n355\t    - Untrained Exit Delta\n356\t    - Training Effect\n357\t    - Interpretation\n358\t    rows:\n359\t    - - LIBERO-Goal\n360\t      - '0.069'\n361\t      - '0.015'\n362\t      - 4.6x\n363\t      - Moderate collapse\n364\t    - - LIBERO-Spatial\n365\t      - '0.040'\n366\t      - '0.023'\n367\t      - 1.7x\n368\t      - Weak collapse, task-dependent\n369\t    - - LIBERO-Object\n370\t      - '0.121'\n371\t      - '0.076'\n372\t      - 1.6x\n373\t      - Moderate but untrained also collapses\n374\t  figures_description:\n375\t  - 'Paired bar chart: Goal vs Spatial exit delta，显示 collapse 强度的 task dependency'\n376\t  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark 结果在 worst tier 下被解读为 exit collapse 是 task-complexity-dependent\n377\t    而非 architectural invariant。如果 collapse 强度随任务变化，它更像是 training-specific adaptation\n378\t    而非 fundamental routing reorganization。Framework reframe 可以 claim \"our framework\n379\t    reveals task-dependent routing intensity\"—— 但这削弱了 \"architecture-independent signature\"\n380\t    的 universality。\n381\t\n382\t    '\n383\t- name: Full-layer R² scan\n384\t  plan_id: plan_011\n385\t  description: 33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 R² 全层扫描\n386\t  expected_results:\n387\t    trained_image_mean_peak:\n388\t      layer: 8\n389\t      R2: 0.655\n390\t    trained_last_preaction_peak:\n391\t      layer: 13\n392\t      R2: 0.678\n393\t    untrained_image_mean_peak:\n394\t      layer: 0\n395\t      R2: 0.64\n396\t    untrained_last_preaction_peak:\n397\t      layer: 32\n398\t      R2: 0.609\n399\t    trained_exit_R2: 0.422\n400\t    untrained_exit_R2: 0.545\n401\t    exit_collapse_delta: 0.123\n402\t    best_vs_best_lastpre_delta: 0.069\n403\t    best_vs_best_lastpre_p: 0.0001\n404\t  result_rationale: '数据不变（OpenVLA 单架构）。这是 R² exit collapse 的源头证据。 Worst D095 下的核心攻击：Reviewer\n405\t    A 论证 \"exit collapse 是 decoder-only LLM 在 supervised fine-tuning 下的通用行为——last preaction\n406\t    token 在 exit layer 被 action head ''consume''，functional information 被转化为 action\n407\t    prediction 而非保留在 hidden state 中。这不是 VLA-specific routing， 而是任何 decoder-only model\n408\t    做 seq2seq mapping 时的 normal information bottleneck。你需要对比 LLM 在 NLP task fine-tuning\n409\t    下的 exit layer R² 来排除这个 confound——但你没做这个 control。\" Reviewer B 补充：\"untrained model（random\n410\t    init）的 last_preaction R² 在 L10-L13 pathological (≈0) 不是 exit collapse 的对照——random\n411\t    init model 在深层的 R²≈0 只是说明随机权重不能解码信息，这与 trained model 的 exit collapse 机制完全不同。你实际上没有一个\n412\t    clean baseline。\"\n413\t\n414\t    '\n415\t  tables:\n416\t  - title: 'R² Exit Collapse: Missing Control (Worst-Tier)'\n417\t    columns:\n418\t    - Condition\n419\t    - Peak R²\n420\t    - Exit R²\n421\t    - Delta\n422\t    - Reviewer Critique\n423\t    rows:\n424\t    - - Trained\n425\t      - 0.678 (L13)\n426\t      - 0.422 (L32)\n427\t      - '0.256'\n428\t      - Could be generic fine-tuning bottleneck\n429\t    - - Untrained (random)\n430\t      - 0.609 (L32)\n431\t      - n/a\n432\t      - n/a\n433\t      - Not a valid control for collapse\n434\t    - - Llama-2 base\n435\t      - 0.645 (L9)\n436\t      - 0.555 (L32)\n437\t      - '0.090'\n438\t      - Base LLM also shows mild decline\n439\t    - - NLP fine-tuned LLM\n440\t      - ???\n441\t      - ???\n442\t      - ???\n443\t      - 'Missing: the critical control'\n444\t  figures_description:\n445\t  - Per-layer R² curve 添加 'NLP fine-tuning control needed' 标注在 gap 区域\n446\t  analysis: 'Worst tier 下 exit collapse 的 VLA-specificity 被根本性质疑。 缺少 NLP fine-tuned\n447\t    LLM 的 per-layer R² control 是最大 gap—— 如果 Llama-2 fine-tuned on any supervised task\n448\t    也显示类似 exit collapse， 那 VLA training 的 \"unique\" contribution 归零。Framework reframe\n449\t    下， collapse 降为 \"one of the patterns our framework detects\"， VLA-specificity claim\n450\t    移除，改为 \"future work: compare across fine-tuning domains\"。\n451\t\n452\t    '\n453\t- name: CLIP-ViT pretraining control\n454\t  plan_id: plan_012\n455\t  description: CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 区分 VL pretraining vs encoder quality\n456\t  expected_results:\n457\t    clip_rsa: 0.557\n458\t    clip_R2: 0.587\n459\t    clip_lt_dino_in_both: true\n460\t    vl_pretraining_not_sufficient: true\n461\t  result_rationale: '数据已完成：CLIP RSA=0.557 < DINO cls=0.692，R²=0.587 < DINO R²=0.634。\n462\t    VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised。Worst D095 下，此结果被 reviewer 进一步延伸：\"你们的 CLIP\n463\t    < DINO 结果说明 vision encoder 质量不取决于 language supervision，那你们为什么还在论文里花大量篇幅讨论 instruction\n464\t    routing？如果最好的 action representation 来自无 language 的 DINO， 那 VLA 的 instruction routing\n465\t    可能是 overhead 而非 feature。\" 这挑战了整篇论文的前提——studying instruction routing in VLA 的意义。\n466\t\n467\t    '\n468\t  tables:\n469\t  - title: 'Encoder Comparison: DINO Dominance Problem'\n470\t    columns:\n471\t    - Encoder\n472\t    - RSA\n473\t    - R²\n474\t    - Has Language?\n475\t    - Worst Implication\n476\t    rows:\n477\t    - - DINO cls\n478\t      - '0.692'\n479\t      - '0.634'\n480\t      - 'No'\n481\t      - Best in both metrics without language\n482\t    - - SigLIP+Proj\n483\t      - '0.615'\n484\t      - '0.630'\n485\t      - 'Yes'\n486\t      - VL pretraining inferior to DINO\n487\t    - - CLIP ViT-L\n488\t      - '0.557'\n489\t      - '0.587'\n490\t      - 'Yes'\n491\t      - VL pretraining worst of three\n492\t    - - Implication\n493\t      - —\n494\t      - —\n495\t      - —\n496\t      - Language supervision hurts encoder quality?\n497\t  figures_description:\n498\t  - 'Scatter plot: RSA vs R² 显示 DINO 独占右上角，两个 VL encoders 均在左下'\n499\t  analysis: 'CLIP 结果在 worst tier 下不仅否定 VL pretraining 的 encoder quality claim， 更挑战论文研究\n500\t    instruction routing 的 motivation：如果最好的 action representations 来自无 language 的 encoder，instruction\n501\t    routing research 的 practical relevance 是什么？Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge 这个\n502\t    tension 并 argue \"understanding routing is important precisely because the relationship\n503\t    between language and action is non-obvious\"。\n504\t\n505\t    '\n506\t- name: Branch-split RSA\n507\t  plan_id: plan_013\n508\t  description: DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 vs SigLIP branch 分离\n509\t  expected_results:\n510\t    dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n511\t    siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n512\t    fused_rsa: 0.634\n513\t    post_projector_rsa: 0.615\n514\t  result_rationale: '数据不变。DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP（Δ<0.002）在 fused backbone 内。 Worst D095 下，此实验仅适用于\n515\t    OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP backbone。 TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision 的不同 vision encoder（SigLIP-based\n516\t    但 架构不同），NORA 用 InternViT。Branch-split analysis 不可迁移到 其他架构。Reviewer：\"这是一个 OpenVLA\n517\t    architecture-specific 的 interesting detail，但对 cross-architecture story 无贡献。\" 在\n518\t    8 页限制下，worst tier 建议移到 appendix。\n519\t\n520\t    '\n521\t  tables: []\n522\t  figures_description: []\n523\t  analysis: 'Framework reframe 下可保留为 appendix 的 \"framework depth demo\"—— 展示 framework\n524\t    能做 sub-encoder-level 分析。但不占 main text 篇幅。\n525\t\n526\t    '\n527\t- name: Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix\n528\t  plan_id: cross_arch_r2_matrix\n529\t  description: 3 架构 × 4 suite 的 R² exit collapse 矩阵——D095 升级的核心证据\n530\t  expected_results:\n531\t    total_matrix_cells: 10\n532\t    cells_with_clear_collapse: 6\n533\t    cells_with_weak_or_absent_collapse: 4\n534\t    openvla_goal_trained_delta: 0.069\n535\t    openvla_spatial_trained_delta: 0.04\n536\t    openvla_object_trained_delta: 0.121\n537\t    openvla_long_trained_delta: 0.004\n538\t    tracvla_goal_trained_delta: 0.09\n539\t    tracvla_spatial_trained_delta: 0.138\n540\t    tracvla_object_trained_delta: 0.294\n541\t    tracvla_long_trained_delta: 0.198\n542\t    nora_goal_trained_delta: 0.691\n543\t    nora_spatial_trained_delta: 0.302\n544\t    mean_trained_exit_delta: 0.096\n545\t    cross_arch_r2_peak_layer_std: 6.2\n546\t    r2_collapse_confirmed_cells: 6\n547\t  result_rationale: 'Worst tier 假设：(1) OpenVLA Spatial（RUNNING）结果弱——exit delta 仅 0.04，\n548\t    远低于其他 cells，且 untrained 也有 0.023 delta，training effect 仅 1.7x。 (2) OpenVLA Long\n549\t    (OFT) delta=0.004 已是 outlier。(3) NORA Object/Long 缺失（无 checkpoint），矩阵只有 10/12\n550\t    cells。(4) 6/10 cells 有 clear collapse（delta>0.10 且 trained>>untrained），但 4 cells\n551\t    弱或例外。\n552\t\n553\t    Reviewer 攻击：\"你们声称 ''architecture-independent'' 但 10 个 cell 中 4 个 不支持。OpenVLA 的\n554\t    2/4 suites 要么 delta≈0 (Long) 要么 delta 很小 (Spatial)。 只有 TracVLA 和 NORA 显示强 collapse——但这两个是你们自己训练的\n555\t    checkpoint 而非社区标准模型。OpenVLA 是唯一的社区 checkpoint，它的结果最弱。 这可能说明 strong exit collapse\n556\t    是你们训练流程的 artifact 而非 VLA training 的 inherent property。\"\n557\t\n558\t    Reviewer B 补充：\"NORA goal delta=0.691 和 spatial delta=0.302 是极端值—— 比其他架构高一个数量级。这种\n559\t    high variance across architectures（std=6.2 in peak layer）说明 exit collapse 的 magnitude\n560\t    高度 architecture-dependent， 而你们只是 cherry-pick 了所有 delta>0 的 cell 来 claim ''consistent''。\n561\t    Consistent direction（都 >0）但 inconsistent magnitude（0.004 到 0.691） ——这不叫 architecture-independent\n562\t    signature，这叫 noisy observation。\"\n563\t\n564\t    '\n565\t  tables:\n566\t  - title: R² Exit Collapse Matrix (Worst-Tier Interpretation)\n567\t    columns:\n568\t    - Architecture\n569\t    - Suite\n570\t    - Trained Delta\n571\t    - Untrained Delta\n572\t    - Ratio\n573\t    - Verdict\n574\t    rows:\n575\t    - - OpenVLA\n576\t      - Goal\n577\t      - '0.069'\n578\t      - '0.015'\n579\t      - 4.6x\n580\t      - Moderate\n581\t    - - OpenVLA\n582\t      - Spatial\n583\t      - '0.040'\n584\t      - '0.023'\n585\t      - 1.7x\n586\t      - Weak — near noise\n587\t    - - OpenVLA\n588\t      - Object\n589\t      - '0.121'\n590\t      - '0.076'\n591\t      - 1.6x\n592\t      - Moderate but untrained also high\n593\t    - - OpenVLA\n594\t      - Long (OFT)\n595\t      - '0.004'\n596\t      - '0.016'\n597\t      - 0.25x\n598\t      - FAIL — no collapse\n599\t    - - TracVLA\n600\t      - Goal\n601\t      - '0.090'\n602\t      - '0.048'\n603\t      - 1.9x\n604\t      - Weak\n605\t    - - TracVLA\n606\t      - Spatial\n607\t      - '0.138'\n608\t      - '0.016'\n609\t      - 8.6x\n610\t      - Strong\n611\t    - - TracVLA\n612\t      - Object\n613\t      - '0.294'\n614\t      - '0.009'\n615\t      - 32.7x\n616\t      - Strong\n617\t    - - TracVLA\n618\t      - Long\n619\t      - '0.198'\n620\t      - '0.028'\n621\t      - 7.1x\n622\t      - Strong\n623\t    - - NORA\n624\t      - Goal\n625\t      - '0.691'\n626\t      - '0.044'\n627\t      - 15.7x\n628\t      - Extreme — outlier?\n629\t    - - NORA\n630\t      - Spatial\n631\t      - '0.302'\n632\t      - '0.037'\n633\t      - 8.2x\n634\t      - Strong\n635\t  - title: Matrix Coverage and Gaps\n636\t    columns:\n637\t    - Metric\n638\t    - Value\n639\t    - Worst Interpretation\n640\t    rows:\n641\t    - - Cells filled\n642\t      - 10/12\n643\t      - NORA Object/Long missing — incomplete\n644\t    - - Clear collapse (>0.10)\n645\t      - 6/10\n646\t      - Only 60% cells show clear effect\n647\t    - - Weak/absent\n648\t      - 4/10\n649\t      - 40% cells ambiguous or failed\n650\t    - - Delta range\n651\t      - 0.004–0.691\n652\t      - 172x range — not 'consistent'\n653\t    - - Peak layer std\n654\t      - '6.2'\n655\t      - High variability in where collapse occurs\n656\t  figures_description:\n657\t  - 'Heatmap: 3×4 matrix 用 color intensity 表示 delta magnitude，4 cells 用虚线边框标注 ''weak/absent''，2\n658\t    cells 灰色标注 ''missing'''\n659\t  - 'Box plot: delta distribution across 10 cells，标注 median=0.096 和 IQR 显示 high spread'\n660\t  analysis: 'Worst tier 核心判定：cross-architecture R² exit collapse 是方向一致的（9/10 trained>untrained）\n661\t    但 magnitude 高度不一致（0.004-0.691）。\"Architecture-independent signature\" claim 在 worst\n662\t    tier 下被降级为 \"a directionally consistent but magnitude-variable observation\"。 Reviewer\n663\t    要求：(1) 解释 magnitude variation 的 mechanism（为什么 NORA 15x 于 OpenVLA？）， (2) 排除 training\n664\t    procedure confound（自训练 vs 社区 checkpoint）， (3) 提供 NLP fine-tuning baseline 排除 decoder-only\n665\t    generic effect。 Framework reframe：exit collapse 降为 \"one of the patterns detected\n666\t    by our framework\" 而非 \"the architecture-independent signature\"。强调 framework 能 systematically\n667\t    reveal cross-architecture variation 而非 uniformity。\n668\t\n669\t    '\n670\t- name: Cross-Architecture L1 Attention (D090 Training-Induced vs Base-Model)\n671\t  plan_id: cross_arch_l1_attention\n672\t  description: 3 架构的 L1 instruction-dominant heads 对比——D090 区分 training vs base-model\n673\t    effects\n674\t  expected_results:\n675\t    openvla_trained_l1_heads: 24\n676\t    openvla_untrained_l1_heads: 0\n677\t    openvla_oxe_l1_heads: 25\n678\t    tracvla_trained_l1_heads:\n679\t    - 27\n680\t    - 30\n681\t    tracvla_untrained_l1_heads: 32\n682\t    nora_trained_l1_heads:\n683\t    - 12\n684\t    - 13\n685\t    nora_untrained_l1_heads:\n686\t    - 13\n687\t    - 14\n688\t    training_induced: false\n689\t    base_model_dependent: true\n690\t  result_rationale: 'D090 发现 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent 而非 training-induced。\n691\t    Worst tier 解读：这是论文最严重的自我削弱。Reviewer：\"你们自己证明了 L1 routing——论文最 visually striking\n692\t    的结果（0→9→24 heads gradient）—— 不是训练学到的。TracVLA untrained 已经 32/32 全极化，NORA untrained\n693\t    已经 13/16。那 VLA training 到底贡献了什么？剩下的 training-induced effects 只有 R² exit collapse\n694\t    和 CF sensitivity。但 exit collapse 可能是 generic fine-tuning effect（见上），CF sensitivity\n695\t    可能只是 ''model produces different outputs for different inputs'' 的 trivial restatement。\n696\t    你们把自己的 contribution 证伪到只剩一个 questionable finding。\"\n697\t\n698\t    D090 被解读为 \"VLA training 的独特效果只剩 exit collapse 一个，contribution 太薄\"。 即使 exit collapse\n699\t    confirmed in 6/10 cells，作为唯一 training-induced effect 支撑一篇 CoRL paper 太单薄。\n700\t\n701\t    '\n702\t  tables:\n703\t  - title: 'L1 Heads: Base-Model Dominance (D090)'\n704\t    columns:\n705\t    - Architecture\n706\t    - Backbone\n707\t    - Trained\n708\t    - Untrained\n709\t    - Training Effect\n710\t    rows:\n711\t    - - OpenVLA\n712\t      - Llama-2-7B\n713\t      - 24/32\n714\t      - 0/32 (random)\n715\t      - 'Artifact: random init has no LM ability'\n716\t    - - OpenVLA\n717\t      - OXE-pretrained\n718\t      - 24/32\n719\t      - 25/32 (OXE)\n720\t      - 'Zero: OXE already saturated'\n721\t    - - TracVLA\n722\t      - Phi-3-mini\n723\t      - 27-30/32\n724\t      - 32/32 (VLM)\n725\t      - 'Negative: training reduces heads'\n726\t    - - NORA\n727\t      - Qwen2.5-VL-3B\n728\t      - 12-13/16\n729\t      - 13-14/16\n730\t      - 'Zero: same before and after'\n731\t  - title: Remaining Training-Induced Effects After D090\n732\t    columns:\n733\t    - Effect\n734\t    - Evidence Strength\n735\t    - VLA-Specificity\n736\t    - Contribution Weight\n737\t    rows:\n738\t    - - R² exit collapse\n739\t      - 6/10 cells\n740\t      - Questionable (need NLP control)\n741\t      - Thin\n742\t    - - CF sensitivity\n743\t      - 11/12 settings\n744\t      - Moderate (empty ≠ original)\n745\t      - Thin\n746\t    - - L1 head count\n747\t      - REMOVED by D090\n748\t      - Base-model artifact\n749\t      - Zero\n750\t    - - Total remaining\n751\t      - —\n752\t      - —\n753\t      - Near-minimal for CoRL\n754\t  figures_description:\n755\t  - 'Before/After D090 contribution diagram: 三个 pillars 砍掉一个，剩两个标注 ''questionable'''\n756\t  analysis: 'D090 在 worst tier 下是论文最大的 self-inflicted wound。Framework reframe 的关键\n757\t    pivot：把 D090 从 \"limitation that weakens the paper\" 转为 \"framework''s key analytical\n758\t    capability\"——\"our framework can distinguish training-induced from pre-existing\n759\t    properties, which is crucial for understanding what VLA training actually does.\"\n760\t    这种 reframe 让 D090 变成 framework 的 selling point 而非 paper 的 weakness。但 reviewer\n761\t    可能看穿这个 rhetorical move。\n762\t\n763\t    '\n764\t- name: Cross-Architecture Counterfactual Sensitivity\n765\t  plan_id: cross_arch_cf\n766\t  description: 3 架构的 counterfactual instruction sensitivity 对比\n767\t  expected_results:\n768\t    openvla_object_d: 1.21\n769\t    tracvla_goal_d: 1.52\n770\t    tracvla_spatial_d: 1.33\n771\t    tracvla_object_d: 1.21\n772\t    tracvla_long_d: 1.47\n773\t    nora_goal_cos_saturated: 1.0\n774\t    cf_sensitivity_ratio_range:\n775\t    - 2\n776\t    - 8\n777\t    empty_always_top: 11/12 settings\n778\t    openvla_long_anomaly: shuffled > empty\n779\t  result_rationale: 'CF sensitivity 是仅存的两个 training-induced effects 之一（D090 后）。 Worst\n780\t    tier 攻击：Reviewer：\"counterfactual sensitivity 只是说 ''trained model produces different\n781\t    outputs for different instructions''——这是 ANY trained language model 的 basic capability，不是\n782\t    VLA-specific routing。你们的 untrained model 是 random init（OpenVLA）或 base VLM without\n783\t    action head（TracVLA/NORA）， 当然 CF sensitivity 低——它们根本不是 functional models。这不是 fair\n784\t    comparison。 一个 fair comparison 是 Llama-2 fine-tuned on NLP 的 counterfactual sensitivity——\n785\t    如果它也显示类似 pattern，那 CF sensitivity 是 instruction following 的 generic property 而非\n786\t    VLA routing。\"\n787\t\n788\t    NORA 的 cosine distance = 1.0（saturated）也有问题——这可能是 numerical artifact 而非 genuine\n789\t    effect（Qwen2.5-VL 的 exit layer 表征可能在不同 instruction 下 彻底 orthogonal 由于某种 architectural\n790\t    reason，而非 VLA training effect）。\n791\t\n792\t    '\n793\t  tables:\n794\t  - title: 'CF Sensitivity: Trained vs Untrained (Worst Interpretation)'\n795\t    columns:\n796\t    - Architecture\n797\t    - Suite\n798\t    - Trained d\n799\t    - Untrained (cos)\n800\t    - Ratio\n801\t    - Reviewer Critique\n802\t    rows:\n803\t    - - OpenVLA\n804\t      - Object\n805\t      - '1.21'\n806\t      - '0.569'\n807\t      - 2.1x\n808\t      - Moderate, within generic fine-tuning range\n809\t    - - TracVLA\n810\t      - Goal\n811\t      - '1.52'\n812\t      - '0.153'\n813\t      - 9.9x\n814\t      - 'Strong but unfair: untrained=VLM base'\n815\t    - - TracVLA\n816\t      - Spatial\n817\t      - '1.33'\n818\t      - '0.180'\n819\t      - 7.4x\n820\t      - Same unfair comparison\n821\t    - - TracVLA\n822\t      - Object\n823\t      - '1.21'\n824\t      - '0.185'\n825\t      - 6.5x\n826\t      - Same unfair comparison\n827\t    - - TracVLA\n828\t      - Long\n829\t      - '1.47'\n830\t      - '0.173'\n831\t      - 8.5x\n832\t      - Same unfair comparison\n833\t    - - NORA\n834\t      - Goal\n835\t      - saturated (1.0)\n836\t      - '0.081'\n837\t      - 12.3x\n838\t      - Numerical artifact? exit layer orthogonal\n839\t  figures_description:\n840\t  - Paired bar chart 标注 'unfair baseline' 在 untrained bars 上\n841\t  analysis: 'CF sensitivity 在 worst tier 下保持 directionally valid 但 fair comparison\n842\t    被质疑。关键缺失控制：NLP-finetuned LLM 的 CF sensitivity。 Framework reframe：CF analysis 降为\n843\t    \"framework capability demonstration\"， future work 建议跨 domain（NLP/vision/robotics）对比\n844\t    CF sensitivity。\n845\t\n846\t    '\n847\t- name: Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)\n848\t  plan_id: three_tier_gradient\n849\t  description: VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA 三层级路由梯度\n850\t  expected_results:\n851\t    tier1_l1_heads:\n852\t    - 0\n853\t    - 32\n854\t    tier1_cf_sensitivity: <0.2\n855\t    tier1_exit_collapse: false\n856\t    tier2_l1_heads: 25\n857\t    tier2_cf_d: 1.048\n858\t    tier2_exit_collapse: false\n859\t    tier3_exit_collapse: true\n860\t    tier3_cf_d:\n861\t    - 1.2\n862\t    - 1.5\n863\t    gradient_narrative: routing emerges at VLM→VLA, reshapes at general→specific\n864\t  result_rationale: '三层级梯度被驳为 post-hoc narrative。Worst tier 核心问题：Tier-2 只有一个 数据点（OpenVLA\n865\t    OXE-pretrained）。Reviewer：\"你们的 three-tier gradient 有 multiple Tier-1 数据点（TracVLA\n866\t    Phi-3-Vision, NORA Qwen2.5-VL）和 multiple Tier-3 数据点（3 arch × 4 suites），但 Tier-2\n867\t    只有 ONE 数据点 （openvla-7b OXE pretrained）。Three-tier gradient 需要 at least 3 intermediate\n868\t    points 才能建立 gradient 而非 step function。你实际上只有 step function：VLM (no routing) →\n869\t    VLA (routing)。''Gradient'' 这个词 暗示 continuous variation，但你只有 binary transition\n870\t    + 1 intermediate。\"\n871\t\n872\t    更致命的是 Tier-2 的 L1 heads（25/32）几乎与 Tier-3（24/32）相同—— D090 已经证明 L1 heads 是 base-model-dependent。所以\n873\t    Tier-2→Tier-3 transition 的 routing 变化主要体现在 exit collapse（有/无）和 CF pattern（general/task-specific）——但这些效应量很小且可能是\n874\t    generic fine-tuning effect。\n875\t\n876\t    三层级叙事的第三个问题：没有第四层（如 multi-task→single-task fine-tuning） 来验证 gradient 是 monotonic\n877\t    的。如果 further specialization 反而 reduces routing（如 libero_finetuned 数据中 L31 exit\n878\t    engagement 18→0）， 那 gradient narrative 不成立——routing 不是 monotonically increasing\n879\t    with specialization。\n880\t\n881\t    '\n882\t  tables:\n883\t  - title: 'Three-Tier Gradient: Data Sparsity (Worst-Tier)'\n884\t    columns:\n885\t    - Tier\n886\t    - Description\n887\t    - N data points\n888\t    - Evidence\n889\t    - Reviewer Critique\n890\t    rows:\n891\t    - - 'Tier 1: VLM base'\n892\t      - No action training\n893\t      - 3 (Phi-3, Qwen2.5, random)\n894\t      - No collapse, low CF\n895\t      - Adequate N\n896\t    - - 'Tier 2: OXE-pretrained'\n897\t      - General action training\n898\t      - 1 (openvla-7b ONLY)\n899\t      - No collapse, strong CF, strong L1\n900\t      - N=1, cannot establish gradient\n901\t    - - 'Tier 3: Task-finetuned'\n902\t      - Task-specific training\n903\t      - ~10 (3 arch × 4 suites)\n904\t      - Collapse + task CF\n905\t      - Adequate N\n906\t    - - Verdict\n907\t      - —\n908\t      - —\n909\t      - —\n910\t      - Step function, not gradient\n911\t  figures_description:\n912\t  - Gradient diagram 中 Tier-2 标注 'N=1' 并用虚线连接，质疑 gradient claim\n913\t  analysis: 'Worst tier 下三层级梯度必须移除或降为 \"preliminary observation\"。 Framework reframe：不\n914\t    claim gradient，改为 \"framework enables comparison across training stages\"——展示 framework\n915\t    能分析不同训练阶段， 但不 claim 发现了 systematic gradient。Future work 建议收集更多 Tier-2 数据点（不同的\n916\t    OXE-pretrained checkpoints、不同的 pretraining datasets）来测试 gradient hypothesis。\n917\t\n918\t    '\n919\t- name: OpenVLA Goal Standardized Pipeline (RUNNING)\n920\t  plan_id: openvla_goal_standardized_v1\n921\t  description: OpenVLA LIBERO-Goal 标准化全流程——统一方法和指标的 re-run\n922\t  expected_results:\n923\t    r2_exit_collapse_delta: 0.07\n924\t    l1_instruction_dominant: 24\n925\t    cf_empty_d: 0.98\n926\t    cf_sensitivity_ratio: 3.5\n927\t    cross_instruction_accuracy: 1.0\n928\t    rsa_peak_layer: 12\n929\t  result_rationale: 'RUNNING 实验。Worst tier 预测：结果与已有 OpenVLA Goal 数据基本一致 （exit delta≈0.07,\n930\t    L1 heads≈24），因为使用相同 checkpoint。 但 standardized pipeline 可能暴露之前分散实验的 inconsistency——\n931\t    例如不同实验使用了略微不同的 hyperparameters（probe architecture, learning rate, seed）导致数字不完全\n932\t    match。Reviewer 会注意到 \"为什么你需要 re-run standardized pipeline？之前的数字不可靠吗？\" 这暗示之前的 ad-hoc\n933\t    实验流程不够 rigorous。 在 worst tier 下，standardized re-run 得到 slightly different numbers\n934\t    (e.g., exit delta 0.07 vs 之前的 0.069) 会被解读为 \"results are hyperparameter-sensitive\"。\n935\t\n936\t    '\n937\t  tables:\n938\t  - title: 'Standardized vs Original: Consistency Check'\n939\t    columns:\n940\t    - Metric\n941\t    - Original\n942\t    - Standardized\n943\t    - Delta\n944\t    - Concern\n945\t    rows:\n946\t    - - R² exit delta\n947\t      - '0.069'\n948\t      - '0.070'\n949\t      - '+0.001'\n950\t      - Consistent but trivial\n951\t    - - L1 instr-dom heads\n952\t      - 24/32\n953\t      - 24/32\n954\t      - '0'\n955\t      - Identical\n956\t    - - CF empty d\n957\t      - '0.968'\n958\t      - '0.980'\n959\t      - '+0.012'\n960\t      - Consistent\n961\t    - - RSA peak\n962\t      - L12\n963\t      - L12\n964\t      - '0'\n965\t      - Identical\n966\t  figures_description: []\n967\t  analysis: 'Standardized pipeline 在 worst tier 下的隐含风险：承认之前的实验 不够 standardized，可能让\n968\t    reviewer 质疑所有之前的数字。 但如果数字高度一致，也可以作为 robustness evidence。 Framework reframe：强调\n969\t    standardized pipeline 是 framework 的 核心贡献之一——\"plug-and-play analysis toolkit\"。\n970\t\n971\t    '\n972\t- name: OpenVLA Spatial Standardized Pipeline (RUNNING)\n973\t  plan_id: openvla_spatial_standardized_v1\n974\t  description: OpenVLA LIBERO-Spatial 标准化全流程\n975\t  expected_results:\n976\t    r2_exit_collapse_delta: 0.04\n977\t    l1_instruction_dominant: 24\n978\t    cf_empty_d: 0.94\n979\t    cf_sensitivity_ratio: 3.0\n980\t    exit_collapse_weak: true\n981\t    matrix_cell_verdict: weak — borderline\n982\t  result_rationale: 'RUNNING 实验，worst tier 核心关注。预测 exit delta 仅 0.04—— 显著弱于 OpenVLA\n983\t    Object (0.121) 和其他架构。原因： (1) LIBERO-Spatial 的 action 空间以位置 reasoning 为主， exit\n984\t    layer 需要保留更多 spatial information 来输出精确 actions， 所以 collapse 较弱。(2) OpenVLA 在 Spatial\n985\t    task 上的 fine-tuning quality 可能较低（Spatial 是最难的 LIBERO suite）， 训练不充分导致 exit reorganization\n986\t    不完全。(3) 如果 untrained 也有 delta≈0.023，则 training effect ratio 仅 1.7x—— 在统计上可能 borderline\n987\t    significant。\n988\t\n989\t    这个结果直接影响 matrix 的 story：OpenVLA 的 4 个 suite 中 2 个（Spatial 0.04, Long 0.004）weak/absent，只有\n990\t    Object (0.121) 和 Goal (0.07) moderate。社区标准 checkpoint 的 2/4 suites 不支持 exit collapse\n991\t    = 严重的 generalizability concern。\n992\t\n993\t    '\n994\t  tables:\n995\t  - title: OpenVLA Cross-Suite Exit Collapse (Worst-Tier)\n996\t    columns:\n997\t    - Suite\n998\t    - Trained Delta\n999\t    - Verdict\n1000\t    - Paper Implication\n1001\t    rows:\n1002\t    - - Goal\n1003\t      - '0.070'\n1004\t      - Moderate\n1005\t      - Supports claim with caveats\n1006\t    - - Spatial\n1007\t      - '0.040'\n1008\t      - Weak\n1009\t      - Borderline — weakens universality\n1010\t    - - Object\n1011\t      - '0.121'\n1012\t      - Moderate-Strong\n1013\t      - Best OpenVLA cell\n1014\t    - - Long (OFT)\n1015\t      - '0.004'\n1016\t      - Absent\n1017\t      - Outlier — OFT confound\n1018\t    - - Overall\n1019\t      - mean=0.059\n1020\t      - Weak-Moderate\n1021\t      - OpenVLA is the WEAKEST architecture\n1022\t  figures_description:\n1023\t  - OpenVLA 4-suite exit collapse bar chart 标注 'community checkpoint' 并与 TracVLA/NORA\n1024\t    对比——OpenVLA consistently lowest\n1025\t  analysis: 'OpenVLA Spatial 弱结果是 worst tier 最关键的预测。如果确认， 论文面临 \"社区 checkpoint 最弱\"\n1026\t    的尴尬叙事——reviewer 会问 \"如果你们用社区标准 checkpoint 复现你们的发现，效果最弱， 这是否说明 strong exit collapse\n1027\t    是你们自训练流程的 artifact？\" Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge OpenVLA 作为 \"weaker case\"\n1028\t    并 argue \"our framework''s value is precisely in revealing such cross-architecture\n1029\t    variation\"。\n1030\t\n1031\t    '\n1032\t- name: D090 Training-Induced vs Base-Model Distinction Synthesis\n1033\t  plan_id: d090_synthesis\n1034\t  description: 综合分析：VLA training 实际贡献了什么——D090 后的 contribution auditing\n1035\t  expected_results:\n1036\t    training_induced_effects:\n1037\t    - R² exit collapse (6/10 cells)\n1038\t    - CF sensitivity (11/12 settings)\n1039\t    base_model_effects:\n1040\t    - L1 head count\n1041\t    - deep-layer probe stability\n1042\t    removed_from_contribution:\n1043\t    - L1 routing gradient (0→9→24)\n1044\t    - attention reorganization\n1045\t    remaining_unique_contribution: thin — 1-2 effects, both questionable VLA-specificity\n1046\t    reviewer_expected_reaction: contribution too thin for CoRL\n1047\t  result_rationale: \"D090 移除了最 visually striking 的结果（L1 head gradient）后， 论文的 unique\\\n1048\t    \\ contribution audit 在 worst tier 下： (1) R² exit collapse — 6/10 cells 确认但 magnitude\\\n1049\t    \\ 高度可变， 可能是 generic fine-tuning effect（缺 NLP control）。 (2) CF sensitivity — 11/12\\\n1050\t    \\ settings trained > untrained， 但 unfair baseline（untrained = random init 或 VLM\\\n1051\t    \\ without action head）。 (3) 三层级梯度 — N=1 at Tier-2，post-hoc narrative。\\n至少 2 个\\\n1052\t    \\ reviewer 给 reject，原因集中在： - \\\"What does VLA training ACTUALLY do that's unique?\\\n1053\t    \\ After your own D090\\n  analysis, the answer is 'exit collapse' — which may not\\\n1054\t    \\ be VLA-specific.\\\"\\n- \\\"Practical value unclear: knowing about exit collapse\\\n1055\t    \\ doesn't help\\n  build better VLAs. No behavioral validation, no design implications\\\n1056\t    \\ tested.\\\"\\n- \\\"The paper's main strength is the experimental framework, not\\\n1057\t    \\ the findings.\\n  But CoRL reviews papers for findings, not frameworks.\\\"\\n\\n\\\n1058\t    Expected reviewer avg score: 3.5 (range 3.0-4.5) Accept probability: 0.10 (range\\\n1059\t    \\ 0.05-0.20)\\n\"\n1060\t  tables:\n1061\t  - title: Contribution Audit After D090 (Worst-Tier)\n1062\t    columns:\n1063\t    - Claimed Contribution\n1064\t    - Status Post-D090\n1065\t    - VLA-Specific?\n1066\t    - Reviewer Verdict\n1067\t    rows:\n1068\t    - - L1 routing (0→9→24)\n1069\t      - REMOVED — base-model artifact\n1070\t      - 'No'\n1071\t      - Cannot claim\n1072\t    - - R² exit collapse\n1073\t      - Retained but 4/10 cells weak\n1074\t      - Questionable\n1075\t      - Need NLP control\n1076\t    - - CF sensitivity\n1077\t      - Retained, 11/12 settings\n1078\t      - Questionable\n1079\t      - Unfair baseline\n1080\t    - - Three-tier gradient\n1081\t      - N=1 at Tier-2\n1082\t      - Thin\n1083\t      - Post-hoc narrative\n1084\t    - - Experimental framework\n1085\t      - Intact\n1086\t      - 'Yes'\n1087\t      - Main contribution in reframe\n1088\t    - - Metric dissociation (RSA/CKA/R²)\n1089\t      - Intact\n1090\t      - 'Yes'\n1091\t      - Methodological\n1092\t  - title: Worst-Tier Reviewer Score Prediction\n1093\t    columns:\n1094\t    - Reviewer\n1095\t    - Score\n1096\t    - Main Concern\n1097\t    - Accept/Reject\n1098\t    rows:\n1099\t    - - R1 (generalizability)\n1100\t      - '3'\n1101\t      - 40% matrix cells weak; no NLP control; contribution too thin\n1102\t      - Reject\n1103\t    - - R2 (methodology)\n1104\t      - '5'\n1105\t      - Framework is solid and reusable; findings secondary but valid\n1106\t      - Weak Accept\n1107\t    - - R3 (practical value)\n1108\t      - '3'\n1109\t      - No behavioral validation; no design implications tested; CoRL wants practical\n1110\t      - Reject\n1111\t    - - Mean\n1112\t      - '3.67'\n1113\t      - 2 reject, 1 weak accept\n1114\t      - Likely Reject\n1115\t  figures_description:\n1116\t  - 'Contribution pyramid: framework at base (strong), exit collapse in middle (questionable),\n1117\t    L1 routing crossed out at top'\n1118\t  analysis: 'Worst tier 核心结论：D090 的 honest analysis 是 scientifically correct 但 strategically\n1119\t    devastating。论文自己证明了 3 个原 claim pillars 中 1 个是 base-model artifact（L1 routing），另外\n1120\t    2 个（exit collapse, CF） 缺少 critical controls。剩余的 unique contribution 太薄支撑 CoRL\n1121\t    paper。\n1122\t\n1123\t    Reframe 路径（accept probability 0.10→0.20 的条件）： (1) C1 升级为主贡献——framework 本身（factorial\n1124\t    design + 4 methods + 3 arch validation） 是可复用工具，CoRL 有 benchmark/framework paper\n1125\t    先例。 (2) R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity 降为 \"findings the framework reveals\"—— 不 claim\n1126\t    VLA-specific，改为 \"training-induced effects observable through our framework\"。 (3)\n1127\t    D090 repackage 为 \"framework''s distinguishing capability\"—— 能区分 training-induced\n1128\t    vs pre-existing 是 framework 的 unique selling point。 (4) 增加 2-3 个 additional analyses（per-layer\n1129\t    information flow entropy, cross-task representation transfer analysis）增强 framework\n1130\t    demonstration value。 (5) 三层级梯度移除或降为 1 段 future work。 (6) 明确 roadmap：\"framework\n1131\t    enables future closed-loop behavioral studies\"。 (7) Title 从 \"Architecture-Independent\n1132\t    Routing in VLAs\" 改为 \"A Systematic Framework for Analyzing Instruction Processing\n1133\t    in VLAs\"。\n1134\t\n1135\t    即使全部执行，worst tier accept probability 仍只 0.05-0.20—— 因为 CoRL 倾向 \"systems + results\"\n1136\t    而非 \"analysis + framework\"。'\n1137\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd00c091-cb94-4a78-804d-87db5c7a2985","uuid":"0cbf187f-ac77-4faa-b8ee-efe6a5b83d33","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:28:27.451Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T021705/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '跨架构证据被质疑为不充分或 trivial。Reviewer 论证 R² exit collapse 是 decoder-only\n  架构的通用表征压缩 而非 VLA-specific effect（\"any supervised fine-tuning on decoder-only LLM\n  would produce similar exit-layer information loss\"）。OpenVLA Spatial 无明显 exit collapse（RUNNING\n  实验结果弱），矩阵空洞（NORA Object/Long 缺失）使 \"architecture-independent\" claim 站不住。D090 的 base-model-dependent\n  发现被解读为 \"contribution 只剩 exit collapse 一个 training-induced effect，太薄\"。三层级梯度仅 1 个\n  Tier-2 数据点（OpenVLA OXE）， 被驳为 post-hoc narrative。Behavioral validation 完全缺失在 CoRL（robotics\n  venue）被视为 near-fatal。 Reframe 方向：从 \"architecture-independent routing signature\"\n  转为 \"systematic diagnostic framework for VLA internal representations\"。C1 (framework)\n  升为主要贡献，R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity 降为 \"findings the framework reveals\"。增加 per-layer\n  information flow entropy、cross-task transfer analysis 等 framework demonstration\n  analyses 增强贡献厚度。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen\n    vision encoder\n  expected_results:\n    siglip_projector_rsa: 0.615\n    trained_with_inst_rsa: 0.488\n    untrained_with_inst_rsa: 0.485\n    dino_rsa: 0.388\n    llm_degradation_delta: 0.127\n  result_rationale: '数据已完成不变。但在 worst D095 下，此实验仅覆盖 OpenVLA 一种架构。Reviewer 攻击： \"SigLIP+DinoSigLIP\n    projector 的 RSA=0.615 是 OpenVLA-specific 的 frozen encoder 观察。 TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision\n    的不同 encoder，NORA 用 InternViT——你们没测这些 encoder 的 RSA。 单架构 encoder analysis 不能 claim\n    architecture-independent。\" 在 framework reframe 下， 此实验降为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上的\n    case study\"，不再是 core contribution。 LLM degradation（0.615→0.488）本身仍有价值但被限定为 \"observed\n    in Llama-2-7B backbone\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: SigLIP RSA Scope Limitation (Worst-Tier)\n    columns:\n    - Source\n    - RSA\n    - Architecture Coverage\n    - Worst Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - SigLIP+Proj\n      - '0.615'\n      - OpenVLA only\n      - Cannot generalize to other VLA encoders\n    - - VLA trained\n      - '0.488'\n      - OpenVLA only\n      - Llama-2 specific LLM degradation\n    - - VLA untrained\n      - '0.485'\n      - OpenVLA only\n      - Random-init Llama-2 specific\n    - - DINO\n      - '0.388'\n      - Standalone\n      - Reference baseline, unaffected\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart 标注 'OpenVLA only' 在每个 bar 上方，突显 single-arch limitation\n  analysis: 'Framework reframe 下此实验从 C1 core evidence 降为 Section 4.1 case study。 价值在于\n    demonstrate framework 的 encoder-LLM decomposition 能力，而非 claim 本身。 Reviewer 不会因此给分但也不会因此扣分——neutral\n    contribution in worst tier。\n\n    '\n- name: DINO baseline RSA\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: Standalone vision model 参照基线\n  expected_results:\n    dino_rsa: 0.388\n    dino_action_R2: 0.687\n    dino_subtask_auc: 0.972\n  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst 档下 DINO 的角色不变——纯视觉 baseline。但 reviewer 可能用 DINO 的高\n    action R²=0.687 攻击论文：\"DINO（self-supervised, 无 language, 无 action training） 的 action\n    probe R² 已 0.687，你们声称的 VLA training-induced R² exit collapse 只是从 0.68 掉到 0.60——这可能只是\n    fine-tuning 过程中正常的 representation compression， 任何 supervised fine-tuning 都会导致\n    exit layer 表征质量下降。\"\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - DINO 作为 'no-training baseline' 的 R²=0.687 标注在所有 cross-arch R² exit collapse 图上，质疑\n    collapse 的意义\n  analysis: 'DINO baseline 在 worst tier 被 reviewer 用来论证 exit collapse 的 trivial nature：\n    如果未训练模型 R²=0.687 而训练后 exit R² 下降到 0.55-0.60，这可能只是 supervised learning 的通用 representation\n    bottleneck 而非 VLA-specific routing。\n\n    '\n- name: Per-layer RSA degradation curve\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\n  expected_results:\n    proj_rsa: 0.615\n    trained_peak_rsa: 0.488\n    trained_peak_layer: 9\n    untrained_peak_rsa: 0.485\n    untrained_peak_layer: 12\n    proj_to_l1_drop: 0.13\n    inverted_u_pattern: true\n  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下，inverted-U pattern 只在 OpenVLA (Llama-2) 上验证。\n    TracVLA 和 NORA 的 RSA per-layer curve 未做（只做了 R² probe），所以 \"inverted-U is architecture-independent\"\n    无法 claim。Reviewer：\"RSA inverted-U 可能是 Llama-2 的 32 层架构特有的——Phi-3-mini 同为 32 层但\n    tokenization 不同，Qwen2.5-VL 是 36 层 且 GQA 架构，per-layer dynamics 可能完全不同。\" 此外 CKA\n    反转（plan_009）使 RSA 本身作为 metric 的 authority 被削弱。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: RSA Inverted-U Architecture Coverage\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - RSA Per-Layer Done?\n    - Pattern\n    - Worst Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\n      - 'Yes'\n      - Inverted-U\n      - Only confirmed case\n    - - TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\n      - 'No'\n      - Unknown\n      - Cannot claim generalization\n    - - NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\n      - 'No'\n      - Unknown\n      - Cannot claim generalization\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-layer RSA curve 只有 OpenVLA 一条线，旁边标 '?' 表示其他架构未验证\n  analysis: 'Framework reframe 下，inverted-U 成为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上发现的 pattern\"\n    而非 \"architecture-independent finding\"。可以保留为 case study 但不能 claim generality。 补救路径：增加\n    TracVLA/NORA 的 per-layer RSA 分析作为 framework demonstration。\n\n    '\n- name: Output head analysis\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\n  expected_results:\n    vision_projector_cos_sim: 1.0\n    llm_rel_change_range:\n    - 1.22\n    - 1.37\n    head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n    shallow_adaptation_gate: FAIL\n  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下，此实验对 framework 贡献有价值——它证明 framework 能 区分 frozen\n    和 trainable 组件。但 reviewer 可能指出：\"这是 trivial verification—— OpenVLA 的训练代码明确 freeze\n    了 vision encoder，你们只是验证了代码做了它说的事。 这不是 experimental finding，是 implementation confirmation。\"\n    在 framework paper 中， 这降为 Section 3 的 methodology validation paragraph，不占独立篇幅。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Worst tier 下此实验贡献接近零——reviewer 视为 trivial。但在 framework reframe 下 可以包装为\n    \"framework 的 component attribution 能力 demonstration\"：展示 framework 如何分离 encoder/projector/LLM\n    各组件的贡献。贡献在方法论而非 finding。\n\n    '\n- name: 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained 表征结构\n  expected_results:\n    trained_vs_untrained_delta: 0.003\n    all_methods_consistent: true\n    cross_benchmark_replicated: true\n  result_rationale: 'Orphaned 但子实验完成。Worst D095 下，trained ≈ untrained 的 RSA 结论仍成立\n    但意义被 D090 reinterpret：Reviewer 说 \"trained ≈ untrained 在 distributed representation\n    (RSA/R²) 上不奇怪——frozen encoder 输出相同 L0 features，LLM 的 fine-tuning 主要影响 exit layer\n    action head，中间层表征 naturally preserved。 这是 transfer learning 的常识，不需要 6 种方法来验证。\"\n    在 framework paper 中， 6 methods consistency 仍是 methodology 亮点——展示 framework 的 multi-method\n    triangulation 能力。但 finding 本身被视为 expected。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 6 Methods Consistency (Worst-Tier Reinterpretation)\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Trained-Untrained Delta\n    - Reviewer Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - RSA\n      - '0.003'\n      - 'Expected: frozen encoder dominates'\n    - - R² probe\n      - '0.015'\n      - 'Expected: similar L0 inputs'\n    - - CKA\n      - '-0.006'\n      - 'Reversal: undermines RSA conclusion'\n    - - Action probe\n      - '0.045'\n      - 'Marginal: routing exists but small'\n    - - Delta probe\n      - '0.011'\n      - 'Expected: similar input structure'\n    - - Classification\n      - '0.001'\n      - Trivially easy for both\n  figures_description:\n  - 6-method radar chart 显示 consistency，但加标注 'Expected under frozen encoder'\n  analysis: 'Worst tier 下 6 methods consistency 从 \"strong evidence for Claim 3\" 降为\n    \"thorough but unsurprising verification\"。Framework reframe 下，价值在于 demonstrate\n    framework 的 multi-method coverage 而非 finding novelty。\n\n    '\n- name: Instruction ablation\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\n  expected_results:\n    delta_with_vs_no_inst: 0.004\n    gate_judgment: FAIL — instruction 无影响 on RSA\n  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下，instruction 对 RSA 无影响是 OpenVLA-specific 观察。\n    Reviewer：\"RSA 测量 image token 的几何结构，当然不受 instruction 影响——image tokens 在 causal\n    mask 下看不到 instruction tokens，这在你们 C1 里已经承认是 structural guarantee。所以 Δ=0.004 不是\n    finding，是 sanity check。\" 更严重的是，TracVLA 和 NORA 上未做此 ablation，所以即使从 framework demonstration\n    角度也只是单架构。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Worst tier 下从 \"Claim 3 evidence\" 降为 \"expected sanity check\"。 但在 framework\n    paper 中，instruction ablation 仍可作为 framework 的 \"controlled manipulation\" capability\n    demonstration，只是不能 claim novelty。\n\n    '\n- name: 2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 四条件全收敛验证\n  expected_results:\n    four_cell_range:\n    - 0.48\n    - 0.49\n    bootstrap_ci_includes_0: true\n    training_effect: 0.003\n    instruction_effect: 0.004\n  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下 2×2 矩阵仍是 clean experimental design 但 被视为 \"confirms\n    the obvious\"。Reviewer：\"frozen encoder + causal mask 已经预测了这个 null result。你的 2×2\n    design 很好但发现的是 expected outcome—— 这不是 contribution，是 verification。\" 在 framework\n    paper 中，2×2 factorial design 可以作为 framework reusability 的 exemplar（\"researchers\n    can apply this factorial approach to any VLA\"），但 the finding itself 不计分。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: '2×2 Matrix (Worst-Tier: Expected Null)'\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - RSA\n    - Reviewer Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Trained + Inst\n      - '0.488'\n      - 'Expected: frozen encoder dominates'\n    - - Trained - Inst\n      - '0.489'\n      - 'Expected: image RSA independent of text'\n    - - Untrained + Inst\n      - '0.485'\n      - 'Expected: same encoder, same RSA'\n    - - Untrained - Inst\n      - '0.480'\n      - 'Expected: null result confirmed'\n  figures_description:\n  - 2×2 heatmap 标注 'Expected null result under frozen encoder hypothesis'\n  analysis: 'Framework paper reframe 下，2×2 matrix 的价值从 \"empirical finding\" 转为 \"exemplar\n    of framework''s factorial design capability\"。论文可以说 \"our framework enables systematic\n    2×2 factorial decomposition of training and instruction effects\"——贡献在方法论可复用性而非结果。\n\n    '\n- name: Random instruction control\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 随机/无意义 instruction 替代验证 RSA 不受 instruction content 影响\n  expected_results:\n    normal_rsa: 0.489\n    random_rsa: 0.484\n    shuffled_rsa: 0.483\n    empty_rsa: 0.472\n    max_absolute_delta: 0.017\n    instruction_invariant: true\n  result_rationale: '数据不变。与 plan_006/007 相同逻辑——causal mask 使 image token RSA 对 instruction\n    天然不变。四种 instruction 条件下 Δ<0.02 是 expected 而非 surprising。 Worst D095 的关键攻击面不在此实验本身，而在于论文用了三个\n    plan（006/007/008） 来验证一个 structurally guaranteed result，reviewer 会认为 \"过度验证 trivial\n    prediction，浪费篇幅\"。在 8 页限制下这 3 个实验应压缩为 1 段。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Framework reframe 下，random instruction control 与 006/007 合并为 \"three-way\n    invariance verification\" 单段，作为 framework sanity check 的示范。占 0.5 段而非独立 subsection。\n\n    '\n- name: CKA verification\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: CKA 指标验证 RSA 发现的 metric robustness\n  expected_results:\n    cka_ordering: untrained > trained > projector > DINO (反转 RSA)\n    rsa_cka_dissociation: true\n    linear_cka_last_preaction: 0.127\n  result_rationale: '数据不变。Worst D095 下 CKA-RSA dissociation 变得更致命。Reviewer： \"你们声称\n    R² exit collapse 是 architecture-independent training effect， 但 CKA（另一种 representational\n    similarity metric）显示 untrained > trained—— 即训练反而增强了 global structure。如果换个 metric\n    就得到相反结论， 那 R² exit collapse 可能只是 metric artifact 而非 genuine information loss。\n    你们怎么证明 R² 比 CKA 更能捕捉 ''action-relevant information''？\" 在 framework paper 中，metric\n    dissociation 可以包装为 \"framework reveals metric-dependent conclusions\"——但这削弱了所有 quantitative\n    findings 的 authority，因为 reviewer 会质疑每个 metric 的选择。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Metric Ordering Reversal (Worst: Authority Crisis)'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Ordering\n    - Implication\n    rows:\n    - - RSA (geometric)\n      - SigLIP > T > U > DINO\n      - Training degrades geometry\n    - - CKA (global)\n      - U > T > SigLIP > DINO\n      - Training preserves/improves structure\n    - - R² (functional)\n      - T_readout > DINO ≈ Proj > T_img\n      - Training enables routing\n    - - Reviewer question\n      - —\n      - Which metric is 'correct' for VLA evaluation?\n  figures_description:\n  - Triple ordering diagram 标注 '?' 在每条 ordering line 上——哪个 metric 才对？\n  analysis: 'Worst tier 下 CKA dissociation 是双刃剑。Framework reframe 可以用它 作为 \"why we\n    need multi-metric frameworks\"（方法论贡献），但这同时 undermine 了 R² exit collapse 作为 \"the\n    architecture-independent signature\" 的 clean narrative。如果 exit collapse 只在 R² 下明显而\n    CKA 下不成立， reviewer 会要求 \"architecture-independent claim 必须 metric-independent\"。\n\n    '\n- name: LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 第三个 benchmark（LIBERO-Spatial）交叉验证\n  expected_results:\n    trained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.696\n    trained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.675\n    untrained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.673\n    untrained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.635\n    trained_exit_R2_delta: 0.04\n    bootstrap_significance_p: 0.001\n    cross_benchmark_consistency: partial\n  result_rationale: 'LIBERO-Spatial 数据已部分完成（plan_010 status=preparing 但 registry 有结果）。\n    Worst D095 下，此实验是 OpenVLA 的 within-architecture cross-benchmark， 不是 cross-architecture\n    validation。Reviewer：\"你从 LIBERO-Goal 换到 LIBERO-Spatial 只是换了 task suite 而非换了 VLA\n    架构——这不解决 RC4 的核心问题。\" 更关键的是，Spatial 的 exit R² delta 只有 0.04（vs Goal 的 0.069）， 说明\n    exit collapse strength 是 task-dependent 的。Worst 解读： exit collapse 不是 fundamental\n    property 而是 task difficulty proxy—— harder tasks (Spatial) 产生较弱 collapse 因为模型需要保留更多\n    exit-layer information 来处理复杂空间推理。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-Benchmark Exit Collapse Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - Trained Exit Delta\n    - Untrained Exit Delta\n    - Training Effect\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - LIBERO-Goal\n      - '0.069'\n      - '0.015'\n      - 4.6x\n      - Moderate collapse\n    - - LIBERO-Spatial\n      - '0.040'\n      - '0.023'\n      - 1.7x\n      - Weak collapse, task-dependent\n    - - LIBERO-Object\n      - '0.121'\n      - '0.076'\n      - 1.6x\n      - Moderate but untrained also collapses\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: Goal vs Spatial exit delta，显示 collapse 强度的 task dependency'\n  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark 结果在 worst tier 下被解读为 exit collapse 是 task-complexity-dependent\n    而非 architectural invariant。如果 collapse 强度随任务变化，它更像是 training-specific adaptation\n    而非 fundamental routing reorganization。Framework reframe 可以 claim \"our framework\n    reveals task-dependent routing intensity\"—— 但这削弱了 \"architecture-independent signature\"\n    的 universality。\n\n    '\n- name: Full-layer R² scan\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 R² 全层扫描\n  expected_results:\n    trained_image_mean_peak:\n      layer: 8\n      R2: 0.655\n    trained_last_preaction_peak:\n      layer: 13\n      R2: 0.678\n    untrained_image_mean_peak:\n      layer: 0\n      R2: 0.64\n    untrained_last_preaction_peak:\n      layer: 32\n      R2: 0.609\n    trained_exit_R2: 0.422\n    untrained_exit_R2: 0.545\n    exit_collapse_delta: 0.123\n    best_vs_best_lastpre_delta: 0.069\n    best_vs_best_lastpre_p: 0.0001\n  result_rationale: '数据不变（OpenVLA 单架构）。这是 R² exit collapse 的源头证据。 Worst D095 下的核心攻击：Reviewer\n    A 论证 \"exit collapse 是 decoder-only LLM 在 supervised fine-tuning 下的通用行为——last preaction\n    token 在 exit layer 被 action head ''consume''，functional information 被转化为 action\n    prediction 而非保留在 hidden state 中。这不是 VLA-specific routing， 而是任何 decoder-only model\n    做 seq2seq mapping 时的 normal information bottleneck。你需要对比 LLM 在 NLP task fine-tuning\n    下的 exit layer R² 来排除这个 confound——但你没做这个 control。\" Reviewer B 补充：\"untrained model（random\n    init）的 last_preaction R² 在 L10-L13 pathological (≈0) 不是 exit collapse 的对照——random\n    init model 在深层的 R²≈0 只是说明随机权重不能解码信息，这与 trained model 的 exit collapse 机制完全不同。你实际上没有一个\n    clean baseline。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'R² Exit Collapse: Missing Control (Worst-Tier)'\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - Peak R²\n    - Exit R²\n    - Delta\n    - Reviewer Critique\n    rows:\n    - - Trained\n      - 0.678 (L13)\n      - 0.422 (L32)\n      - '0.256'\n      - Could be generic fine-tuning bottleneck\n    - - Untrained (random)\n      - 0.609 (L32)\n      - n/a\n      - n/a\n      - Not a valid control for collapse\n    - - Llama-2 base\n      - 0.645 (L9)\n      - 0.555 (L32)\n      - '0.090'\n      - Base LLM also shows mild decline\n    - - NLP fine-tuned LLM\n      - ???\n      - ???\n      - ???\n      - 'Missing: the critical control'\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-layer R² curve 添加 'NLP fine-tuning control needed' 标注在 gap 区域\n  analysis: 'Worst tier 下 exit collapse 的 VLA-specificity 被根本性质疑。 缺少 NLP fine-tuned\n    LLM 的 per-layer R² control 是最大 gap—— 如果 Llama-2 fine-tuned on any supervised task\n    也显示类似 exit collapse， 那 VLA training 的 \"unique\" contribution 归零。Framework reframe\n    下， collapse 降为 \"one of the patterns our framework detects\"， VLA-specificity claim\n    移除，改为 \"future work: compare across fine-tuning domains\"。\n\n    '\n- name: CLIP-ViT pretraining control\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 区分 VL pretraining vs encoder quality\n  expected_results:\n    clip_rsa: 0.557\n    clip_R2: 0.587\n    clip_lt_dino_in_both: true\n    vl_pretraining_not_sufficient: true\n  result_rationale: '数据已完成：CLIP RSA=0.557 < DINO cls=0.692，R²=0.587 < DINO R²=0.634。\n    VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised。Worst D095 下，此结果被 reviewer 进一步延伸：\"你们的 CLIP\n    < DINO 结果说明 vision encoder 质量不取决于 language supervision，那你们为什么还在论文里花大量篇幅讨论 instruction\n    routing？如果最好的 action representation 来自无 language 的 DINO， 那 VLA 的 instruction routing\n    可能是 overhead 而非 feature。\" 这挑战了整篇论文的前提——studying instruction routing in VLA 的意义。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Encoder Comparison: DINO Dominance Problem'\n    columns:\n    - Encoder\n    - RSA\n    - R²\n    - Has Language?\n    - Worst Implication\n    rows:\n    - - DINO cls\n      - '0.692'\n      - '0.634'\n      - 'No'\n      - Best in both metrics without language\n    - - SigLIP+Proj\n      - '0.615'\n      - '0.630'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - VL pretraining inferior to DINO\n    - - CLIP ViT-L\n      - '0.557'\n      - '0.587'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - VL pretraining worst of three\n    - - Implication\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n      - Language supervision hurts encoder quality?\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: RSA vs R² 显示 DINO 独占右上角，两个 VL encoders 均在左下'\n  analysis: 'CLIP 结果在 worst tier 下不仅否定 VL pretraining 的 encoder quality claim， 更挑战论文研究\n    instruction routing 的 motivation：如果最好的 action representations 来自无 language 的 encoder，instruction\n    routing research 的 practical relevance 是什么？Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge 这个\n    tension 并 argue \"understanding routing is important precisely because the relationship\n    between language and action is non-obvious\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Branch-split RSA\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 vs SigLIP branch 分离\n  expected_results:\n    dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n    siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n    fused_rsa: 0.634\n    post_projector_rsa: 0.615\n  result_rationale: '数据不变。DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP（Δ<0.002）在 fused backbone 内。 Worst D095 下，此实验仅适用于\n    OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP backbone。 TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision 的不同 vision encoder（SigLIP-based\n    但 架构不同），NORA 用 InternViT。Branch-split analysis 不可迁移到 其他架构。Reviewer：\"这是一个 OpenVLA\n    architecture-specific 的 interesting detail，但对 cross-architecture story 无贡献。\" 在\n    8 页限制下，worst tier 建议移到 appendix。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Framework reframe 下可保留为 appendix 的 \"framework depth demo\"—— 展示 framework\n    能做 sub-encoder-level 分析。但不占 main text 篇幅。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix\n  plan_id: cross_arch_r2_matrix\n  description: 3 架构 × 4 suite 的 R² exit collapse 矩阵——D095 升级的核心证据\n  expected_results:\n    total_matrix_cells: 10\n    cells_with_clear_collapse: 6\n    cells_with_weak_or_absent_collapse: 4\n    openvla_goal_trained_delta: 0.069\n    openvla_spatial_trained_delta: 0.04\n    openvla_object_trained_delta: 0.121\n    openvla_long_trained_delta: 0.004\n    tracvla_goal_trained_delta: 0.09\n    tracvla_spatial_trained_delta: 0.138\n    tracvla_object_trained_delta: 0.294\n    tracvla_long_trained_delta: 0.198\n    nora_goal_trained_delta: 0.691\n    nora_spatial_trained_delta: 0.302\n    mean_trained_exit_delta: 0.096\n    cross_arch_r2_peak_layer_std: 6.2\n    r2_collapse_confirmed_cells: 6\n  result_rationale: 'Worst tier 假设：(1) OpenVLA Spatial（RUNNING）结果弱——exit delta 仅 0.04，\n    远低于其他 cells，且 untrained 也有 0.023 delta，training effect 仅 1.7x。 (2) OpenVLA Long\n    (OFT) delta=0.004 已是 outlier。(3) NORA Object/Long 缺失（无 checkpoint），矩阵只有 10/12\n    cells。(4) 6/10 cells 有 clear collapse（delta>0.10 且 trained>>untrained），但 4 cells\n    弱或例外。\n\n    Reviewer 攻击：\"你们声称 ''architecture-independent'' 但 10 个 cell 中 4 个 不支持。OpenVLA 的\n    2/4 suites 要么 delta≈0 (Long) 要么 delta 很小 (Spatial)。 只有 TracVLA 和 NORA 显示强 collapse——但这两个是你们自己训练的\n    checkpoint 而非社区标准模型。OpenVLA 是唯一的社区 checkpoint，它的结果最弱。 这可能说明 strong exit collapse\n    是你们训练流程的 artifact 而非 VLA training 的 inherent property。\"\n\n    Reviewer B 补充：\"NORA goal delta=0.691 和 spatial delta=0.302 是极端值—— 比其他架构高一个数量级。这种\n    high variance across architectures（std=6.2 in peak layer）说明 exit collapse 的 magnitude\n    高度 architecture-dependent， 而你们只是 cherry-pick 了所有 delta>0 的 cell 来 claim ''consistent''。\n    Consistent direction（都 >0）但 inconsistent magnitude（0.004 到 0.691） ——这不叫 architecture-independent\n    signature，这叫 noisy observation。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: R² Exit Collapse Matrix (Worst-Tier Interpretation)\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - Suite\n    - Trained Delta\n    - Untrained Delta\n    - Ratio\n    - Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - Goal\n      - '0.069'\n      - '0.015'\n      - 4.6x\n      - Moderate\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - Spatial\n      - '0.040'\n      - '0.023'\n      - 1.7x\n      - Weak — near noise\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - Object\n      - '0.121'\n      - '0.076'\n      - 1.6x\n      - Moderate but untrained also high\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - Long (OFT)\n      - '0.004'\n      - '0.016'\n      - 0.25x\n      - FAIL — no collapse\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Goal\n      - '0.090'\n      - '0.048'\n      - 1.9x\n      - Weak\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Spatial\n      - '0.138'\n      - '0.016'\n      - 8.6x\n      - Strong\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Object\n      - '0.294'\n      - '0.009'\n      - 32.7x\n      - Strong\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Long\n      - '0.198'\n      - '0.028'\n      - 7.1x\n      - Strong\n    - - NORA\n      - Goal\n      - '0.691'\n      - '0.044'\n      - 15.7x\n      - Extreme — outlier?\n    - - NORA\n      - Spatial\n      - '0.302'\n      - '0.037'\n      - 8.2x\n      - Strong\n  - title: Matrix Coverage and Gaps\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    - Worst Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Cells filled\n      - 10/12\n      - NORA Object/Long missing — incomplete\n    - - Clear collapse (>0.10)\n      - 6/10\n      - Only 60% cells show clear effect\n    - - Weak/absent\n      - 4/10\n      - 40% cells ambiguous or failed\n    - - Delta range\n      - 0.004–0.691\n      - 172x range — not 'consistent'\n    - - Peak layer std\n      - '6.2'\n      - High variability in where collapse occurs\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: 3×4 matrix 用 color intensity 表示 delta magnitude，4 cells 用虚线边框标注 ''weak/absent''，2\n    cells 灰色标注 ''missing'''\n  - 'Box plot: delta distribution across 10 cells，标注 median=0.096 和 IQR 显示 high spread'\n  analysis: 'Worst tier 核心判定：cross-architecture R² exit collapse 是方向一致的（9/10 trained>untrained）\n    但 magnitude 高度不一致（0.004-0.691）。\"Architecture-independent signature\" claim 在 worst\n    tier 下被降级为 \"a directionally consistent but magnitude-variable observation\"。 Reviewer\n    要求：(1) 解释 magnitude variation 的 mechanism（为什么 NORA 15x 于 OpenVLA？）， (2) 排除 training\n    procedure confound（自训练 vs 社区 checkpoint）， (3) 提供 NLP fine-tuning baseline 排除 decoder-only\n    generic effect。 Framework reframe：exit collapse 降为 \"one of the patterns detected\n    by our framework\" 而非 \"the architecture-independent signature\"。强调 framework 能 systematically\n    reveal cross-architecture variation 而非 uniformity。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-Architecture L1 Attention (D090 Training-Induced vs Base-Model)\n  plan_id: cross_arch_l1_attention\n  description: 3 架构的 L1 instruction-dominant heads 对比——D090 区分 training vs base-model\n    effects\n  expected_results:\n    openvla_trained_l1_heads: 24\n    openvla_untrained_l1_heads: 0\n    openvla_oxe_l1_heads: 25\n    tracvla_trained_l1_heads:\n    - 27\n    - 30\n    tracvla_untrained_l1_heads: 32\n    nora_trained_l1_heads:\n    - 12\n    - 13\n    nora_untrained_l1_heads:\n    - 13\n    - 14\n    training_induced: false\n    base_model_dependent: true\n  result_rationale: 'D090 发现 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent 而非 training-induced。\n    Worst tier 解读：这是论文最严重的自我削弱。Reviewer：\"你们自己证明了 L1 routing——论文最 visually striking\n    的结果（0→9→24 heads gradient）—— 不是训练学到的。TracVLA untrained 已经 32/32 全极化，NORA untrained\n    已经 13/16。那 VLA training 到底贡献了什么？剩下的 training-induced effects 只有 R² exit collapse\n    和 CF sensitivity。但 exit collapse 可能是 generic fine-tuning effect（见上），CF sensitivity\n    可能只是 ''model produces different outputs for different inputs'' 的 trivial restatement。\n    你们把自己的 contribution 证伪到只剩一个 questionable finding。\"\n\n    D090 被解读为 \"VLA training 的独特效果只剩 exit collapse 一个，contribution 太薄\"。 即使 exit collapse\n    confirmed in 6/10 cells，作为唯一 training-induced effect 支撑一篇 CoRL paper 太单薄。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'L1 Heads: Base-Model Dominance (D090)'\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - Backbone\n    - Trained\n    - Untrained\n    - Training Effect\n    rows:\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - Llama-2-7B\n      - 24/32\n      - 0/32 (random)\n      - 'Artifact: random init has no LM ability'\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - OXE-pretrained\n      - 24/32\n      - 25/32 (OXE)\n      - 'Zero: OXE already saturated'\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Phi-3-mini\n      - 27-30/32\n      - 32/32 (VLM)\n      - 'Negative: training reduces heads'\n    - - NORA\n      - Qwen2.5-VL-3B\n      - 12-13/16\n      - 13-14/16\n      - 'Zero: same before and after'\n  - title: Remaining Training-Induced Effects After D090\n    columns:\n    - Effect\n    - Evidence Strength\n    - VLA-Specificity\n    - Contribution Weight\n    rows:\n    - - R² exit collapse\n      - 6/10 cells\n      - Questionable (need NLP control)\n      - Thin\n    - - CF sensitivity\n      - 11/12 settings\n      - Moderate (empty ≠ original)\n      - Thin\n    - - L1 head count\n      - REMOVED by D090\n      - Base-model artifact\n      - Zero\n    - - Total remaining\n      - —\n      - —\n      - Near-minimal for CoRL\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Before/After D090 contribution diagram: 三个 pillars 砍掉一个，剩两个标注 ''questionable'''\n  analysis: 'D090 在 worst tier 下是论文最大的 self-inflicted wound。Framework reframe 的关键\n    pivot：把 D090 从 \"limitation that weakens the paper\" 转为 \"framework''s key analytical\n    capability\"——\"our framework can distinguish training-induced from pre-existing\n    properties, which is crucial for understanding what VLA training actually does.\"\n    这种 reframe 让 D090 变成 framework 的 selling point 而非 paper 的 weakness。但 reviewer\n    可能看穿这个 rhetorical move。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-Architecture Counterfactual Sensitivity\n  plan_id: cross_arch_cf\n  description: 3 架构的 counterfactual instruction sensitivity 对比\n  expected_results:\n    openvla_object_d: 1.21\n    tracvla_goal_d: 1.52\n    tracvla_spatial_d: 1.33\n    tracvla_object_d: 1.21\n    tracvla_long_d: 1.47\n    nora_goal_cos_saturated: 1.0\n    cf_sensitivity_ratio_range:\n    - 2\n    - 8\n    empty_always_top: 11/12 settings\n    openvla_long_anomaly: shuffled > empty\n  result_rationale: 'CF sensitivity 是仅存的两个 training-induced effects 之一（D090 后）。 Worst\n    tier 攻击：Reviewer：\"counterfactual sensitivity 只是说 ''trained model produces different\n    outputs for different instructions''——这是 ANY trained language model 的 basic capability，不是\n    VLA-specific routing。你们的 untrained model 是 random init（OpenVLA）或 base VLM without\n    action head（TracVLA/NORA）， 当然 CF sensitivity 低——它们根本不是 functional models。这不是 fair\n    comparison。 一个 fair comparison 是 Llama-2 fine-tuned on NLP 的 counterfactual sensitivity——\n    如果它也显示类似 pattern，那 CF sensitivity 是 instruction following 的 generic property 而非\n    VLA routing。\"\n\n    NORA 的 cosine distance = 1.0（saturated）也有问题——这可能是 numerical artifact 而非 genuine\n    effect（Qwen2.5-VL 的 exit layer 表征可能在不同 instruction 下 彻底 orthogonal 由于某种 architectural\n    reason，而非 VLA training effect）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'CF Sensitivity: Trained vs Untrained (Worst Interpretation)'\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - Suite\n    - Trained d\n    - Untrained (cos)\n    - Ratio\n    - Reviewer Critique\n    rows:\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - Object\n      - '1.21'\n      - '0.569'\n      - 2.1x\n      - Moderate, within generic fine-tuning range\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Goal\n      - '1.52'\n      - '0.153'\n      - 9.9x\n      - 'Strong but unfair: untrained=VLM base'\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Spatial\n      - '1.33'\n      - '0.180'\n      - 7.4x\n      - Same unfair comparison\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Object\n      - '1.21'\n      - '0.185'\n      - 6.5x\n      - Same unfair comparison\n    - - TracVLA\n      - Long\n      - '1.47'\n      - '0.173'\n      - 8.5x\n      - Same unfair comparison\n    - - NORA\n      - Goal\n      - saturated (1.0)\n      - '0.081'\n      - 12.3x\n      - Numerical artifact? exit layer orthogonal\n  figures_description:\n  - Paired bar chart 标注 'unfair baseline' 在 untrained bars 上\n  analysis: 'CF sensitivity 在 worst tier 下保持 directionally valid 但 fair comparison\n    被质疑。关键缺失控制：NLP-finetuned LLM 的 CF sensitivity。 Framework reframe：CF analysis 降为\n    \"framework capability demonstration\"， future work 建议跨 domain（NLP/vision/robotics）对比\n    CF sensitivity。\n\n    '\n- name: Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)\n  plan_id: three_tier_gradient\n  description: VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA 三层级路由梯度\n  expected_results:\n    tier1_l1_heads:\n    - 0\n    - 32\n    tier1_cf_sensitivity: <0.2\n    tier1_exit_collapse: false\n    tier2_l1_heads: 25\n    tier2_cf_d: 1.048\n    tier2_exit_collapse: false\n    tier3_exit_collapse: true\n    tier3_cf_d:\n    - 1.2\n    - 1.5\n    gradient_narrative: routing emerges at VLM→VLA, reshapes at general→specific\n  result_rationale: '三层级梯度被驳为 post-hoc narrative。Worst tier 核心问题：Tier-2 只有一个 数据点（OpenVLA\n    OXE-pretrained）。Reviewer：\"你们的 three-tier gradient 有 multiple Tier-1 数据点（TracVLA\n    Phi-3-Vision, NORA Qwen2.5-VL）和 multiple Tier-3 数据点（3 arch × 4 suites），但 Tier-2\n    只有 ONE 数据点 （openvla-7b OXE pretrained）。Three-tier gradient 需要 at least 3 intermediate\n    points 才能建立 gradient 而非 step function。你实际上只有 step function：VLM (no routing) →\n    VLA (routing)。''Gradient'' 这个词 暗示 continuous variation，但你只有 binary transition\n    + 1 intermediate。\"\n\n    更致命的是 Tier-2 的 L1 heads（25/32）几乎与 Tier-3（24/32）相同—— D090 已经证明 L1 heads 是 base-model-dependent。所以\n    Tier-2→Tier-3 transition 的 routing 变化主要体现在 exit collapse（有/无）和 CF pattern（general/task-specific）——但这些效应量很小且可能是\n    generic fine-tuning effect。\n\n    三层级叙事的第三个问题：没有第四层（如 multi-task→single-task fine-tuning） 来验证 gradient 是 monotonic\n    的。如果 further specialization 反而 reduces routing（如 libero_finetuned 数据中 L31 exit\n    engagement 18→0）， 那 gradient narrative 不成立——routing 不是 monotonically increasing\n    with specialization。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Three-Tier Gradient: Data Sparsity (Worst-Tier)'\n    columns:\n    - Tier\n    - Description\n    - N data points\n    - Evidence\n    - Reviewer Critique\n    rows:\n    - - 'Tier 1: VLM base'\n      - No action training\n      - 3 (Phi-3, Qwen2.5, random)\n      - No collapse, low CF\n      - Adequate N\n    - - 'Tier 2: OXE-pretrained'\n      - General action training\n      - 1 (openvla-7b ONLY)\n      - No collapse, strong CF, strong L1\n      - N=1, cannot establish gradient\n    - - 'Tier 3: Task-finetuned'\n      - Task-specific training\n      - ~10 (3 arch × 4 suites)\n      - Collapse + task CF\n      - Adequate N\n    - - Verdict\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n      - Step function, not gradient\n  figures_description:\n  - Gradient diagram 中 Tier-2 标注 'N=1' 并用虚线连接，质疑 gradient claim\n  analysis: 'Worst tier 下三层级梯度必须移除或降为 \"preliminary observation\"。 Framework reframe：不\n    claim gradient，改为 \"framework enables comparison across training stages\"——展示 framework\n    能分析不同训练阶段， 但不 claim 发现了 systematic gradient。Future work 建议收集更多 Tier-2 数据点（不同的\n    OXE-pretrained checkpoints、不同的 pretraining datasets）来测试 gradient hypothesis。\n\n    '\n- name: OpenVLA Goal Standardized Pipeline (RUNNING)\n  plan_id: openvla_goal_standardized_v1\n  description: OpenVLA LIBERO-Goal 标准化全流程——统一方法和指标的 re-run\n  expected_results:\n    r2_exit_collapse_delta: 0.07\n    l1_instruction_dominant: 24\n    cf_empty_d: 0.98\n    cf_sensitivity_ratio: 3.5\n    cross_instruction_accuracy: 1.0\n    rsa_peak_layer: 12\n  result_rationale: 'RUNNING 实验。Worst tier 预测：结果与已有 OpenVLA Goal 数据基本一致 （exit delta≈0.07,\n    L1 heads≈24），因为使用相同 checkpoint。 但 standardized pipeline 可能暴露之前分散实验的 inconsistency——\n    例如不同实验使用了略微不同的 hyperparameters（probe architecture, learning rate, seed）导致数字不完全\n    match。Reviewer 会注意到 \"为什么你需要 re-run standardized pipeline？之前的数字不可靠吗？\" 这暗示之前的 ad-hoc\n    实验流程不够 rigorous。 在 worst tier 下，standardized re-run 得到 slightly different numbers\n    (e.g., exit delta 0.07 vs 之前的 0.069) 会被解读为 \"results are hyperparameter-sensitive\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Standardized vs Original: Consistency Check'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Original\n    - Standardized\n    - Delta\n    - Concern\n    rows:\n    - - R² exit delta\n      - '0.069'\n      - '0.070'\n      - '+0.001'\n      - Consistent but trivial\n    - - L1 instr-dom heads\n      - 24/32\n      - 24/32\n      - '0'\n      - Identical\n    - - CF empty d\n      - '0.968'\n      - '0.980'\n      - '+0.012'\n      - Consistent\n    - - RSA peak\n      - L12\n      - L12\n      - '0'\n      - Identical\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Standardized pipeline 在 worst tier 下的隐含风险：承认之前的实验 不够 standardized，可能让\n    reviewer 质疑所有之前的数字。 但如果数字高度一致，也可以作为 robustness evidence。 Framework reframe：强调\n    standardized pipeline 是 framework 的 核心贡献之一——\"plug-and-play analysis toolkit\"。\n\n    '\n- name: OpenVLA Spatial Standardized Pipeline (RUNNING)\n  plan_id: openvla_spatial_standardized_v1\n  description: OpenVLA LIBERO-Spatial 标准化全流程\n  expected_results:\n    r2_exit_collapse_delta: 0.04\n    l1_instruction_dominant: 24\n    cf_empty_d: 0.94\n    cf_sensitivity_ratio: 3.0\n    exit_collapse_weak: true\n    matrix_cell_verdict: weak — borderline\n  result_rationale: 'RUNNING 实验，worst tier 核心关注。预测 exit delta 仅 0.04—— 显著弱于 OpenVLA\n    Object (0.121) 和其他架构。原因： (1) LIBERO-Spatial 的 action 空间以位置 reasoning 为主， exit\n    layer 需要保留更多 spatial information 来输出精确 actions， 所以 collapse 较弱。(2) OpenVLA 在 Spatial\n    task 上的 fine-tuning quality 可能较低（Spatial 是最难的 LIBERO suite）， 训练不充分导致 exit reorganization\n    不完全。(3) 如果 untrained 也有 delta≈0.023，则 training effect ratio 仅 1.7x—— 在统计上可能 borderline\n    significant。\n\n    这个结果直接影响 matrix 的 story：OpenVLA 的 4 个 suite 中 2 个（Spatial 0.04, Long 0.004）weak/absent，只有\n    Object (0.121) 和 Goal (0.07) moderate。社区标准 checkpoint 的 2/4 suites 不支持 exit collapse\n    = 严重的 generalizability concern。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: OpenVLA Cross-Suite Exit Collapse (Worst-Tier)\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - Trained Delta\n    - Verdict\n    - Paper Implication\n    rows:\n    - - Goal\n      - '0.070'\n      - Moderate\n      - Supports claim with caveats\n    - - Spatial\n      - '0.040'\n      - Weak\n      - Borderline — weakens universality\n    - - Object\n      - '0.121'\n      - Moderate-Strong\n      - Best OpenVLA cell\n    - - Long (OFT)\n      - '0.004'\n      - Absent\n      - Outlier — OFT confound\n    - - Overall\n      - mean=0.059\n      - Weak-Moderate\n      - OpenVLA is the WEAKEST architecture\n  figures_description:\n  - OpenVLA 4-suite exit collapse bar chart 标注 'community checkpoint' 并与 TracVLA/NORA\n    对比——OpenVLA consistently lowest\n  analysis: 'OpenVLA Spatial 弱结果是 worst tier 最关键的预测。如果确认， 论文面临 \"社区 checkpoint 最弱\"\n    的尴尬叙事——reviewer 会问 \"如果你们用社区标准 checkpoint 复现你们的发现，效果最弱， 这是否说明 strong exit collapse\n    是你们自训练流程的 artifact？\" Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge OpenVLA 作为 \"weaker case\"\n    并 argue \"our framework''s value is precisely in revealing such cross-architecture\n    variation\"。\n\n    '\n- name: D090 Training-Induced vs Base-Model Distinction Synthesis\n  plan_id: d090_synthesis\n  description: 综合分析：VLA training 实际贡献了什么——D090 后的 contribution auditing\n  expected_results:\n    training_induced_effects:\n    - R² exit collapse (6/10 cells)\n    - CF sensitivity (11/12 settings)\n    base_model_effects:\n    - L1 head count\n    - deep-layer probe stability\n    removed_from_contribution:\n    - L1 routing gradient (0→9→24)\n    - attention reorganization\n    remaining_unique_contribution: thin — 1-2 effects, both questionable VLA-specificity\n    reviewer_expected_reaction: contribution too thin for CoRL\n  result_rationale: \"D090 移除了最 visually striking 的结果（L1 head gradient）后， 论文的 unique\\\n    \\ contribution audit 在 worst tier 下： (1) R² exit collapse — 6/10 cells 确认但 magnitude\\\n    \\ 高度可变， 可能是 generic fine-tuning effect（缺 NLP control）。 (2) CF sensitivity — 11/12\\\n    \\ settings trained > untrained， 但 unfair baseline（untrained = random init 或 VLM\\\n    \\ without action head）。 (3) 三层级梯度 — N=1 at Tier-2，post-hoc narrative。\\n至少 2 个\\\n    \\ reviewer 给 reject，原因集中在： - \\\"What does VLA training ACTUALLY do that's unique?\\\n    \\ After your own D090\\n  analysis, the answer is 'exit collapse' — which may not\\\n    \\ be VLA-specific.\\\"\\n- \\\"Practical value unclear: knowing about exit collapse\\\n    \\ doesn't help\\n  build better VLAs. No behavioral validation, no design implications\\\n    \\ tested.\\\"\\n- \\\"The paper's main strength is the experimental framework, not\\\n    \\ the findings.\\n  But CoRL reviews papers for findings, not frameworks.\\\"\\n\\n\\\n    Expected reviewer avg score: 3.5 (range 3.0-4.5) Accept probability: 0.10 (range\\\n    \\ 0.05-0.20)\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: Contribution Audit After D090 (Worst-Tier)\n    columns:\n    - Claimed Contribution\n    - Status Post-D090\n    - VLA-Specific?\n    - Reviewer Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - L1 routing (0→9→24)\n      - REMOVED — base-model artifact\n      - 'No'\n      - Cannot claim\n    - - R² exit collapse\n      - Retained but 4/10 cells weak\n      - Questionable\n      - Need NLP control\n    - - CF sensitivity\n      - Retained, 11/12 settings\n      - Questionable\n      - Unfair baseline\n    - - Three-tier gradient\n      - N=1 at Tier-2\n      - Thin\n      - Post-hoc narrative\n    - - Experimental framework\n      - Intact\n      - 'Yes'\n      - Main contribution in reframe\n    - - Metric dissociation (RSA/CKA/R²)\n      - Intact\n      - 'Yes'\n      - Methodological\n  - title: Worst-Tier Reviewer Score Prediction\n    columns:\n    - Reviewer\n    - Score\n    - Main Concern\n    - Accept/Reject\n    rows:\n    - - R1 (generalizability)\n      - '3'\n      - 40% matrix cells weak; no NLP control; contribution too thin\n      - Reject\n    - - R2 (methodology)\n      - '5'\n      - Framework is solid and reusable; findings secondary but valid\n      - Weak Accept\n    - - R3 (practical value)\n      - '3'\n      - No behavioral validation; no design implications tested; CoRL wants practical\n      - Reject\n    - - Mean\n      - '3.67'\n      - 2 reject, 1 weak accept\n      - Likely Reject\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Contribution pyramid: framework at base (strong), exit collapse in middle (questionable),\n    L1 routing crossed out at top'\n  analysis: 'Worst tier 核心结论：D090 的 honest analysis 是 scientifically correct 但 strategically\n    devastating。论文自己证明了 3 个原 claim pillars 中 1 个是 base-model artifact（L1 routing），另外\n    2 个（exit collapse, CF） 缺少 critical controls。剩余的 unique contribution 太薄支撑 CoRL\n    paper。\n\n    Reframe 路径（accept probability 0.10→0.20 的条件）： (1) C1 升级为主贡献——framework 本身（factorial\n    design + 4 methods + 3 arch validation） 是可复用工具，CoRL 有 benchmark/framework paper\n    先例。 (2) R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity 降为 \"findings the framework reveals\"—— 不 claim\n    VLA-specific，改为 \"training-induced effects observable through our framework\"。 (3)\n    D090 repackage 为 \"framework''s distinguishing capability\"—— 能区分 training-induced\n    vs pre-existing 是 framework 的 unique selling point。 (4) 增加 2-3 个 additional analyses（per-layer\n    information flow entropy, cross-task representation transfer analysis）增强 framework\n    demonstration value。 (5) 三层级梯度移除或降为 1 段 future work。 (6) 明确 roadmap：\"framework\n    enables future closed-loop behavioral studies\"。 (7) Title 从 \"Architecture-Independent\n    Routing in VLAs\" 改为 \"A Systematic Framework for Analyzing Instruction Processing\n    in VLAs\"。\n\n    即使全部执行，worst tier accept probability 仍只 0.05-0.20—— 因为 CoRL 倾向 \"systems + results\"\n    而非 \"analysis + framework\"。'\n","numLines":1137,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1137}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WvHRLJGcF5DoX3iQ4EXTvG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found relevant information about CoRL 2026, though I found limited specific details about a dedicated \"reviewer guidelines review form\" document.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**Author Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and who has at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n**Review Process:**\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**Historical Guidance:**\nWhile I didn't find specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines, I did find CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines that suggest reviewers should evaluate whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, and whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested.\n\nThe search results don't show a specific publicly available \"reviewer guidelines review form\" for CoRL 2026. You may want to check the OpenReview platform directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or contact the CoRL organizers for more detailed reviewer guidelines and forms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd00c091-cb94-4a78-804d-87db5c7a2985","uuid":"6e9fda3a-e4bd-4059-8635-e7abd90f02a2","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:28:31.960Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013DDFHJUhxjSHGRxyDb7Zv8","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on my search results, I found relevant information about CoRL 2026, though I found limited specific details about a dedicated \"reviewer guidelines review form\" document.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**Author Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and who has at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n**Review Process:**\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**Historical Guidance:**\nWhile I didn't find specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines, I did find CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines that suggest reviewers should evaluate whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, and whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested.\n\nThe search results don't show a specific publicly available \"reviewer guidelines review form\" for CoRL 2026. You may want to check the OpenReview platform directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or contact the CoRL organizers for more detailed reviewer guidelines and forms."],"durationSeconds":6.230816882000003}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01898vunwrQh89MKf9RkMXZX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information, but the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric wasn't fully detailed in these results. However, I can share what I found:\n\nFrom the search results, I found reference to CoRL's reviewing process and some guidance. For regular papers, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe search results also show that papers can be desk rejected for formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope, where scope requires all CoRL submissions to demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nAdditionally, CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the complete CoRL 2025 review form with the detailed scoring rubric. For the most current and comprehensive reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric for CoRL 2025, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 website on OpenReview or contacting the conference organizers directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd00c091-cb94-4a78-804d-87db5c7a2985","uuid":"8235520e-6fa2-44eb-ae76-6867d4ede821","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:28:32.037Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QdvQzxuuX7RhMXc56NfjiM","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information, but the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric wasn't fully detailed in these results. However, I can share what I found:\n\nFrom the search results, I found reference to CoRL's reviewing process and some guidance. For regular papers, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe search results also show that papers can be desk rejected for formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope, where scope requires all CoRL submissions to demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nAdditionally, CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the complete CoRL 2025 review form with the detailed scoring rubric. For the most current and comprehensive reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric for CoRL 2025, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 website on OpenReview or contacting the conference organizers directly."],"durationSeconds":5.802255733000002}}
