{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FphjeZRLuEro4JW6es9hPR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 \"instruction for reviews\" reviewer scoring scale accept reject site:2024.corl.org\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instructions for Presentations\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instructions-for-presentations\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Call for Workshops\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-workshops\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Demos\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/demos\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Papers\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Program\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program\"}]\n\nI found the CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page. However, the search results show information about evaluation criteria and reviewer qualifications, but do not contain a specific reviewer scoring scale with accept/reject options. \n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nACs will identify the desk rejection candidates, using specified criteria as justification, and the PC will examine the candidates and make the final decision.\n\nThe search results from the instructions page don't explicitly detail a numbered or labeled scoring scale (such as 1-5 or accept/reject/borderline options). To find the complete scoring scale, you may need to access the full Instructions for Reviews page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews or check the OpenReview submission platform where the detailed reviewer guidelines may be hosted.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd00c091-cb94-4a78-804d-87db5c7a2985","uuid":"e8e3a42b-3946-4f22-bbc3-6eef458cfbea","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:28:45.908Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 \"instruction for reviews\" reviewer scoring scale accept reject site:2024.corl.org","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01PguFWdGRbbGQ282mL9jrzg","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2024","url":"https://2024.corl.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instructions for Presentations","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instructions-for-presentations"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Call for Papers","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Call for Workshops","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-workshops"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Demos","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/demos"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Papers","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Program","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program"}]},"I found the CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page. However, the search results show information about evaluation criteria and reviewer qualifications, but do not contain a specific reviewer scoring scale with accept/reject options. \n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nACs will identify the desk rejection candidates, using specified criteria as justification, and the PC will examine the candidates and make the final decision.\n\nThe search results from the instructions page don't explicitly detail a numbered or labeled scoring scale (such as 1-5 or accept/reject/borderline options). To find the complete scoring scale, you may need to access the full Instructions for Reviews page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews or check the OpenReview submission platform where the detailed reviewer guidelines may be hosted."],"durationSeconds":7.312187894999996}}
