{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MoVCVDnPq1TJ75pNGdKrTZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL openreview review form \"overall score\" \"1:\" \"2:\" \"3:\" rating scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Paper Ranking Methodology\",\"url\":\"https://openreview-copilot.eamag.me/ranking\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"Why are the \\\"rating\\\" and \\\"confidence\\\" fields in my PC Console wrong? | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/getting-started/frequently-asked-questions/why-are-the-rating-and-confidence-fields-in-my-pc-console-wrong\"},{\"title\":\"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OpenReview's default review form rating scale. The OpenReview default form includes a rating scale with values from 1 to 10, where 1 represents \"Trivial or wrong,\" 2 represents \"Strong rejection,\" 3 represents \"Clear rejection,\" and continuing up to 10 which represents \"Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper.\"\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about a CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning)-specific review form with the exact format you specified (\"1:\" \"2:\" \"3:\" etc.). The results show the general OpenReview default form structure, but not a CoRL-customized version. To get the specific CoRL review form details, you might want to check the CoRL conference website directly or contact their organizers, as different conferences may customize their review forms on OpenReview.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd00c091-cb94-4a78-804d-87db5c7a2985","uuid":"5b26ad90-722c-42ef-bec7-4f01644e8744","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:28:54.592Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL openreview review form \"overall score\" \"1:\" \"2:\" \"3:\" rating scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CP8Tn47NEGoJxpZx4wBxgH","content":[{"title":"Default Review Form | OpenReview","url":"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Paper Ranking Methodology","url":"https://openreview-copilot.eamag.me/ranking"},{"title":"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions"},{"title":"Why are the \"rating\" and \"confidence\" fields in my PC Console wrong? | OpenReview","url":"https://docs.openreview.net/getting-started/frequently-asked-questions/why-are-the-rating-and-confidence-fields-in-my-pc-console-wrong"},{"title":"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about OpenReview's default review form rating scale. The OpenReview default form includes a rating scale with values from 1 to 10, where 1 represents \"Trivial or wrong,\" 2 represents \"Strong rejection,\" 3 represents \"Clear rejection,\" and continuing up to 10 which represents \"Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper.\"\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about a CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning)-specific review form with the exact format you specified (\"1:\" \"2:\" \"3:\" etc.). The results show the general OpenReview default form structure, but not a CoRL-customized version. To get the specific CoRL review form details,